"commandPaletteRegister(\"export\", \"Export PDF\", \"\", () => "
"exportPdf());\n"
"// then:\n"
"commandPaletteShow();\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:579
msgid "MapView (issue #517)"
msgstr "MapView (issue #517)"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:581
msgid ""
"Wraps `MKMapView` on macOS / iOS / visionOS / tvOS, `libshumate` on GTK4, "
"Google Maps SDK on Android (requires API key in `AndroidManifest.xml`), the "
"SwiftUI `Map` view on watchOS, and the native Windows `MapControl` in a XAML "
"Island. On Windows, obtain a Bing Maps key as described in Microsoft's [maps "
"authentication guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/uwp/maps-and-"
"location/authentication-key), then set `PERRY_MAP_SERVICE_TOKEN` (or the "
"legacy `PERRY_BING_MAPS_KEY` alias) before launching the app. The token is "
"read when each MapView is created and assigned to "
"`MapControl.MapServiceToken`."
msgstr ""
"Enveloppe `MKMapView` sur macOS / iOS / visionOS / tvOS, `libshumate` sur "
"GTK4, SDK Google Maps sur Android (requiert une clé API dans "
"`AndroidManifest.xml`), la vue SwiftUI `Map` sur watchOS, et le natif "
"Windows `MapControl` dans une île XAML. Sur Windows, obtenez une clé Bing "
"Maps comme décrit dans [Guide d'authentification des cartes](https://"
"learn.microsoft.com/windows/uwp/maps-and-location/authentication-key) de "
"Microsoft, puis définissez `PERRY_MAP_SERVICE_TOKEN` (ou l'alias "
"`PERRY_BING_MAPS_KEY` hérité) avant de lancer l'application. Le jeton est lu "
"lorsque chaque MapView est créé et attribué à `MapControl.MapServiceToken`."

#: src/ui/widgets.md:590
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  MapView,\n"
"  mapViewSetRegion,\n"
"  mapViewAddPin,\n"
"  mapViewSetMapType,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\";\n"
"\n"
"const map = MapView(800, 600);\n"
"mapViewSetRegion(map, 37.7749, -122.4194, 0.05, 0.05);\n"
"mapViewAddPin(map, 37.7749, -122.4194, \"San Francisco\");\n"
"mapViewSetMapType(map, 1); // 0=standard, 1=satellite, 2=hybrid\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  MapView,\n"
"  mapViewSetRegion,\n"
"  mapViewAddPin,\n"
"  mapViewSetMapType,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\";\n"
"\n"
"const map = MapView(800, 600);\n"
"mapViewSetRegion(map, 37.7749, -122.4194, 0.05, 0.05);\n"
"mapViewAddPin(map, 37.7749, -122.4194, \"San Francisco\");\n"
"mapViewSetMapType(map, 1); // 0=standard, 1=satellite, 2=hybrid\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:604
msgid "PdfView (issue #516)"
msgstr "PdfView (issue #516)"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:606
msgid ""
"Native PDF rendering uses PDFKit on macOS / iOS / visionOS and "
"`Windows.Data.Pdf` with a GDI+ page surface on Windows. `pdfViewLoadFile` "
"returns 1 on success, 0 on failure. Page navigation and zoom redraw real "
"document pixels on both backends."
msgstr ""
"Le rendu PDF natif utilise PDFKit sur macOS / iOS / visionOS et "
"`Windows.Data.Pdf` avec une surface de page GDI + sur Windows. "
"`pdfViewLoadFile` renvoie 1 sur le succès, 0 sur l'échec. Navigation de page "
"et zoom redessiner les vrais pixels du document sur les deux backends."

#: src/ui/widgets.md:611
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  PdfView,\n"
"  pdfViewLoadFile,\n"
"  pdfViewGetPageCount,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\";\n"
"\n"
"const pdf = PdfView(800, 600);\n"
"if (pdfViewLoadFile(pdf, \"/tmp/report.pdf\")) {\n"
"  console.log(\"pages:\", pdfViewGetPageCount(pdf));\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  PdfView,\n"
"  pdfViewLoadFile,\n"
"  pdfViewGetPageCount,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\";\n"
"\n"
"const pdf = PdfView(800, 600);\n"
"if (pdfViewLoadFile(pdf, \"/tmp/report.pdf\")) {\n"
"  console.log(\"pages:\", pdfViewGetPageCount(pdf));\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:624
msgid "RichTextEditor (issue #478)"
msgstr "RichTextEditor (issue #478)"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:626
msgid ""
"`NSTextView` with `NSAttributedString` storage on macOS. Plain-text and HTML "
"round-trip cover persistence; `richTextToggleBold` / `ToggleItalic` / "
"`ToggleUnderline` cover inline formatting via `NSResponder` actions."
msgstr ""
"`NSTextView` avec stockage `NSAttributedString` sur macOS. L'aller-retour "
"texte brut et HTML couvre la persistance ; `richTextToggleBold` / "
"`ToggleItalic` / `ToggleUnderline` couvrent la mise en forme en ligne via "
"les actions `NSResponder`."

#: src/ui/widgets.md:631
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  RichTextEditor,\n"
"  richTextSetHtml,\n"
"  richTextGetHtml,\n"
"  richTextToggleBold,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\";\n"
"\n"
"const editor = RichTextEditor(600, 400, (text) => console.log(text));\n"
"richTextSetHtml(editor, \"<p>Hello <b>world</b></p>\");\n"
"richTextToggleBold(editor);\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import {\n"
"  RichTextEditor,\n"
"  richTextSetHtml,\n"
"  richTextGetHtml,\n"
"  richTextToggleBold,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\";\n"
"\n"
"const editor = RichTextEditor(600, 400, (text) => console.log(text));\n"
"richTextSetHtml(editor, \"<p>Hello <b>world</b></p>\");\n"
"richTextToggleBold(editor);\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:644
msgid "Rich tooltip (issue #479)"
msgstr "Info-bulle enrichie (issue #479)"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:646
msgid ""
"`widgetSetRichTooltip(widget, content, hoverDelayMs)` — like "
"`widgetSetTooltip` but the tooltip content is itself a Perry widget. macOS "
"uses `NSPanel` + `NSTrackingArea`; other platforms stub. For plain-text "
"tooltips with VoiceOver / a11y support, prefer the simpler "
"`widgetSetTooltip`."
msgstr ""
"`widgetSetRichTooltip(widget, content, hoverDelayMs)` — comme "
"`widgetSetTooltip`, mais le contenu de l'info-bulle est lui-même un widget "
"Perry. macOS utilise `NSPanel` + `NSTrackingArea` ; les autres plateformes "
"sont en mode stub. Pour les info-bulles en texte brut avec support "
"VoiceOver / a11y, préférez le plus simple `widgetSetTooltip`."

#: src/ui/widgets.md:652
msgid "WebView (issue #658)"
msgstr "WebView (issue #658)"

#: src/ui/widgets.md:654
msgid ""
"`WebView({ url, allowedDomains?, onShouldNavigate?, ... })` embeds a real "
"browser engine — `WKWebView` on Apple, `WebView2` on Windows, `WebKitGTK "
"6.0` on Linux, `android.webkit.WebView` on Android, sandboxed `<iframe>` on "
"web. See [WebView](webview.md) for the full OAuth / callback-interception "
"pattern and the per-platform notes."
msgstr ""
"`WebView({ url, allowedDomains?, onShouldNavigate?, ... })` intègre un vrai "
"moteur de navigateur — `WKWebView` sur Apple, `WebView2` sur Windows, "
"`WebKitGTK 6.0` sur Linux, `android.webkit.WebView` sur Android, `<iframe>` "
"en bac à sable sur le web. Consultez [WebView](webview.md) pour le schéma "
"complet OAuth / interception de callback et les notes par plateforme."

