#: src/ui/webview.md:3
msgid ""
"`WebView` embeds a real browser engine inside the native widget tree — "
"`WKWebView` on Apple platforms, `WebView2` on Windows, `WebKitGTK 6.0` on "
"Linux, `android.webkit.WebView` on Android, and a sandboxed `<iframe>` on "
"the web target. Use it for OAuth / payment flows, embedded admin pages, "
"help / docs viewers, or any \"show this URL as part of my app\" surface. The "
"cross-platform implementation shipped under closed issue \\#658."
msgstr ""
"`WebView` intègre un véritable moteur de navigateur dans l'arbre de widget "
"natif  `WKWebView` sur les plateformes Apple, `WebView2` sur Windows, "
"`WebKitGTK 6.0` sur Linux, `android.webkit.WebView` sur Android, et un "
"`<iframe>` dans un bac à sable sur la cible Web. Utilisez-le pour les flux "
"OAuth / paiement, les pages d'administration intégrées, les visualiseurs "
"d'aide / documents ou toute surface \"afficher cette URL dans mon "
"application\". La mise en œuvre multiplateforme est livrée sous la version "
"fermée \\#658."

#: src/ui/webview.md:11
msgid ""
"```ts\n"
"import {\n"
"    WebView,\n"
"    webviewLoadUrl,\n"
"    webviewReload,\n"
"    webviewGoBack,\n"
"    webviewGoForward,\n"
"    webviewCanGoBack,\n"
"    webviewEvaluateJs,\n"
"    webviewClearCookies,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```ts\n"
"import {\n"
"    WebView,\n"
"    webviewLoadUrl,\n"
"    webviewReload,\n"
"    webviewGoBack,\n"
"    webviewGoForward,\n"
"    webviewCanGoBack,\n"
"    webviewEvaluateJs,\n"
"    webviewClearCookies,\n"
"} from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/webview.md:24
msgid ""
"**Scope.** This is a \"browser tab embedded in your native widget tree\" "
"primitive — explicit non-goals: a Tauri / Electron-style native↔JS RPC "
"bridge, custom protocol / scheme handlers, DevTools, file downloads, WebGL / "
"camera / mic / clipboard permission negotiation, service workers, WebRTC. If "
"you need any of those, reach for Tauri or Electron; the rest of `perry/ui` "
"still applies."
msgstr ""
"**Périmètre.** Il s'agit d'un primitif « onglet de navigateur intégré dans "
"l'arborescence native de widgets » — objectifs explicitement hors "
"périmètre : un pont RPC natif↔JS de type Tauri / Electron, des gestionnaires "
"de protocoles / schémas personnalisés, DevTools, les téléchargements de "
"fichiers, WebGL / caméra / micro / presse-papiers (négociation de "
"permissions), les service workers, WebRTC. Si vous avez besoin de l'un de "
"ces éléments, utilisez Tauri ou Electron ; le reste de `perry/ui` s'applique "
"toujours."

#: src/ui/webview.md:33
msgid ""
"```ts\n"
"const wv = WebView({\n"
"    url: \"https://example.com\",\n"
"    width: 800,\n"
"    height: 600,\n"
"})\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"WebView Demo\",\n"
"    width: 820,\n"
"    height: 640,\n"
"    body: wv,\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```ts\n"
"const wv = WebView({\n"
"    url: \"https://example.com\",\n"
"    width: 800,\n"
"    height: 600,\n"
"})\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"WebView Demo\",\n"
"    width: 820,\n"
"    height: 640,\n"
"    body: wv,\n"
"})\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/webview.md:48
msgid ""
"`WebView({...})` returns a `Widget` you can drop into any layout container. "
"The widget tree's layout engine controls final size — `width` and `height` "
"are hints for the initial bounds."
msgstr ""
"`WebView({...})` renvoie un `Widget` que vous pouvez insérer dans n'importe "
"quel conteneur de mise en page. Le moteur de mise en page de l'arborescence "
"de widgets contrôle la taille finale — `width` et `height` sont des "
"indications pour les dimensions initiales."

#: src/ui/webview.md:52
msgid "OAuth / Callback Interception"
msgstr "Interception OAuth / Callback"

#: src/ui/webview.md:54
msgid ""
"The load-bearing use case. `onShouldNavigate` is a **synchronous** intercept "
"invoked before each navigation; return `false` to cancel the load. Every "
"backend's should-load hook is itself sync on the main thread "
"(`decidePolicyForNavigationAction`, `NavigationStarting`, "
"`shouldOverrideUrlLoading`, `decide-policy`), so the contract is the same "
"everywhere."
msgstr ""
"Le cas d'usage principal. `onShouldNavigate` est un intercepteur "
"**synchrone** invoqué avant chaque navigation ; retournez `false` pour "
"annuler le chargement. Le hook de contrôle de chargement de chaque backend "
"est lui-même synchrone sur le thread principal "
"(`decidePolicyForNavigationAction`, `NavigationStarting`, "
"`shouldOverrideUrlLoading`, `decide-policy`), de sorte que le contrat est "
"identique partout."

#: src/ui/webview.md:61
msgid ""
"```ts\n"
"const authCode = State(\"\")\n"
"\n"
"const auth = WebView({\n"
"    url: \"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?"
"client_id=...&redirect_uri=https://myapp.com/oauth/"
"callback&response_type=code&scope=email\",\n"
"    // Hard host-level allowlist — blocked at the native delegate\n"
"    // without round-tripping into TS. Exact match or subdomain match\n"
"    // (so \"google.com\" allows \"accounts.google.com\").\n"
"    allowedDomains: [\"accounts.google.com\", \"google.com\", "
"\"myapp.com\"],\n"
"    onShouldNavigate: (url) => {\n"
"        if (url.startsWith(\"https://myapp.com/oauth/callback?\")) {\n"
"            const code = new URL(url).searchParams.get(\"code\") ?? \"\"\n"
"            authCode.set(code)\n"
"            return false  // cancel — we already have what we need\n"
"        }\n"
"        return true\n"
"    },\n"
"    onLoaded: (url) => {\n"
"        // Fires after every successful page load.\n"
"    },\n"
"    onError: (code, message) => {\n"
"        // DNS / TLS / HTTP / cancellation all flow here.\n"
"    },\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```ts\n"
"const authCode = State(\"\")\n"
"\n"
"const auth = WebView({\n"
"    url: \"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?"
"client_id=...&redirect_uri=https://myapp.com/oauth/"
"callback&response_type=code&scope=email\",\n"
"    // Hard host-level allowlist — blocked at the native delegate\n"
"    // without round-tripping into TS. Exact match or subdomain match\n"
"    // (so \"google.com\" allows \"accounts.google.com\").\n"
"    allowedDomains: [\"accounts.google.com\", \"google.com\", "
"\"myapp.com\"],\n"
"    onShouldNavigate: (url) => {\n"
"        if (url.startsWith(\"https://myapp.com/oauth/callback?\")) {\n"
"            const code = new URL(url).searchParams.get(\"code\") ?? \"\"\n"
"            authCode.set(code)\n"
"            return false  // cancel — we already have what we need\n"
"        }\n"
"        return true\n"
"    },\n"
"    onLoaded: (url) => {\n"
"        // Fires after every successful page load.\n"
"    },\n"
"    onError: (code, message) => {\n"
"        // DNS / TLS / HTTP / cancellation all flow here.\n"
"    },\n"
"})\n"
"```"

#: src/ui/webview.md:87
msgid ""
"The `allowedDomains` allowlist is enforced at the **native delegate layer** "
"— disallowed hosts never reach your `onShouldNavigate`. Treat it as defense-"
"in-depth against a hijacked OAuth page redirecting the embedded session "
"somewhere unexpected."
msgstr ""
"La liste d'autorisation `allowedDomains` est appliquée au niveau de la "
"**couche déléguée native** — les hôtes non autorisés n'atteignent jamais "
"votre `onShouldNavigate`. Considérez-la comme une défense en profondeur "
"contre une page OAuth compromise qui redirigerait la session intégrée vers "
"un endroit inattendu."

#: src/ui/webview.md:92
msgid "Imperative Navigation"
msgstr "Navigation impérative"

#: src/ui/webview.md:94
msgid ""
"Drive the WebView from outside (toolbar buttons, deep links, app-state "
"changes):"
msgstr ""
"Pilotez le WebView depuis l'extérieur (boutons de barre d'outils, liens "
"profonds, changements d'état de l'application) :"

#: src/ui/webview.md:97
msgid ""
"```ts\n"
"// Navigate the WebView from outside (e.g. from a toolbar button).\n"
"webviewLoadUrl(wv, \"https://perryts.com\")\n"
