"tableau parallèle à `tabs` — seul le body de l'onglet actif est rendu."

#: src/tui/widgets.md:161
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const [active, setActive] = useState(0);\n"
"Tabs({\n"
"    tabs: [\"Files\", \"Search\", \"Settings\"],\n"
"    active,\n"
"    body: [filesView, searchView, settingsView],\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const [active, setActive] = useState(0);\n"
"Tabs({\n"
"    tabs: [\"Files\", \"Search\", \"Settings\"],\n"
"    active,\n"
"    body: [filesView, searchView, settingsView],\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/widgets.md:172
msgid ""
"For state + event hooks (the React-shape `useState`/`useInput`/`useApp`/"
"etc.), see [Hooks](hooks.md). For complete worked examples, see [Examples]"
"(examples.md)."
msgstr ""
"Pour les hooks d'état et d'événements (l'API façon React `useState`/"
"`useInput`/`useApp`/etc.), voir [Hooks](hooks.md). Pour des exemples "
"complets et fonctionnels, voir [Exemples](examples.md)."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:3
msgid ""
"`perry/tui` implements the React-shape hook API on top of a call-site-"
"indexed slot pool. Each `useXxx` call gets the slot at its position in the "
"component body; the run loop resets the index at the top of every frame, so "
"the second render's `useState` at the same position reads back what the "
"first wrote."
msgstr ""
"`perry/tui` implémente l'API de hooks façon React au-dessus d'un pool de "
"slots indexés par site d'appel. Chaque appel `useXxx` obtient le slot à sa "
"position dans le corps du composant ; la boucle d'exécution réinitialise "
"l'index au début de chaque frame, de sorte que le `useState` de la deuxième "
"passe à la même position relit ce que la première a écrit."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:5
msgid ""
"This is the same rule-of-hooks model ink/React use: **call hooks in the same "
"order on every render**. Don't call them inside `if`/loops — the slot index "
"would skew and you'd read the wrong slot. Slot kinds are tagged (`State` / "
"`Effect` / `Memo` / `Ref` / `Focus`); calling `useState` at a position "
"previously used by `useMemo` re-tags the slot rather than corrupting it, but "
"the value resets."
msgstr ""
"C'est le même modèle de règles de hooks qu'ink/React : **appelez les hooks "
"dans le même ordre à chaque rendu**. Ne les appelez pas dans des `if`/"
"boucles — l'index de slot serait décalé et vous liriez le mauvais slot. Les "
"types de slots sont étiquetés (`State` / `Effect` / `Memo` / `Ref` / "
"`Focus`) ; appeler `useState` à une position précédemment utilisée par "
"`useMemo` réétiquette le slot plutôt que de le corrompre, mais la valeur est "
"réinitialisée."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:7
msgid "`useState(initial)`"
msgstr "`useState(initial)`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:9
msgid "Per-frame state cell. Returns `[value, setter]`."
msgstr "Cellule d'état par frame. Retourne `[value, setter]`."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:11
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n"
"// Later, from an input handler:\n"
"setCount(count + 1);\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n"
"// Later, from an input handler:\n"
"setCount(count + 1);\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:17
msgid ""
"The setter writes through to the slot's bits and flips a global "
"`STATE_DIRTY` flag — the run loop sees it after `useInput` drains and "
"immediately re-renders without sleeping."
msgstr ""
"Le setter écrit directement dans les bits du slot et active un flag global "
"`STATE_DIRTY` — la boucle d'exécution le détecte après que `useInput` ait "
"tout traité et effectue immédiatement un nouveau rendu sans attendre."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:19
msgid ""
"Setting the same value twice (bit-identical) is a no-op — `STATE_DIRTY` "
"stays clear and the loop idles. This avoids the \"render storm\" pattern "
"where unconditional `setX(prev)` calls would loop forever."
msgstr ""
"Définir deux fois la même valeur (identique bit à bit) est un no-op — "
"`STATE_DIRTY` reste inactif et la boucle est en veille. Cela évite le "
"pattern « tempête de rendus » où des appels inconditionnels à `setX(prev)` "
"boucleraient indéfiniment."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:21
msgid "Stale-closure gotcha"
msgstr "Piège de la closure périmée"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:23
msgid ""
"The setter captured by a `useInput` handler reads `value` from **that "
"frame's closure**, not from the slot. If many bytes arrive in one frame "
"(paste, typing fast), the handler fires N times with the same `value`:"
msgstr ""
"Le setter capturé par un handler `useInput` lit `value` depuis **la closure "
"de cette frame**, pas depuis le slot. Si de nombreux octets arrivent en une "
"seule frame (coller du texte, frappe rapide), le handler se déclenche N fois "
"avec le même `value` :"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:25
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const [n, setN] = useState(0);\n"
"useInput((s) => { if (s === \"+\") setN(n + 1); });\n"
"// User pastes \"+++\" — handler fires 3× with n=0, all three set the slot "
"to 1.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const [n, setN] = useState(0);\n"
"useInput((s) => { if (s === \"+\") setN(n + 1); });\n"
"// User pastes \"+++\" — handler fires 3× with n=0, all three set the slot "
"to 1.\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:31
msgid ""
"If you need a functional setter for this case, use `useRef` as a mirror:"
msgstr ""
"Si vous avez besoin d'un setter fonctionnel pour ce cas, utilisez `useRef` "
"comme miroir :"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:33
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const buf = useRef(\"\");\n"
"const [, redraw] = useState(0);\n"
"useInput((s) => {\n"
"    if (s.length === 1 && s >= \" \" && s <= \"~\") {\n"
"        buf.set(buf.get() + s);     // canonical buffer (no stale capture)\n"
"        redraw(buf.get().length);   // trigger re-render\n"
"    }\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const buf = useRef(\"\");\n"
"const [, redraw] = useState(0);\n"
"useInput((s) => {\n"
"    if (s.length === 1 && s >= \" \" && s <= \"~\") {\n"
"        buf.set(buf.get() + s);     // canonical buffer (no stale capture)\n"
"        redraw(buf.get().length);   // trigger re-render\n"
"    }\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:44
msgid "`useEffect(fn, deps?)`"
msgstr "`useEffect(fn, deps?)`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:46
msgid "Run a side effect after first render, and again whenever a dep changes."
msgstr ""
"Exécute un effet de bord après le premier rendu, puis à chaque fois qu'une "
"dépendance change."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:48
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"useEffect(() => {\n"
"    // Run-once on mount.\n"
"    fetchInitialData();\n"
"}, []);\n"
"\n"
"useEffect(() => {\n"
"    // Re-run whenever `query` changes.\n"
"    runSearch(query);\n"
"}, [query]);\n"
"\n"
"useEffect(() => {\n"
"    // No deps array → run every render. Rarely what you want.\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"useEffect(() => {\n"
"    // Run-once on mount.\n"
"    fetchInitialData();\n"
"}, []);\n"
"\n"
"useEffect(() => {\n"
"    // Re-run whenever `query` changes.\n"
"    runSearch(query);\n"
"}, [query]);\n"
"\n"
"useEffect(() => {\n"
"    // No deps array → run every render. Rarely what you want.\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:64
msgid ""
"Deps are compared by bit-identity using an FNV-1a hash of the deps' NaN-"
"boxed values. An empty array `[]` hashes to a stable non-zero value, giving "
"the React \"run once\" behaviour; passing no array runs the effect every "
"render."
msgstr ""
"Les dépendances sont comparées par identité de bits à l'aide d'un hash "
"FNV-1a des valeurs NaN-boxed des dépendances. Un tableau vide `[]` est hashé "
"vers une valeur stable non nulle, ce qui donne le comportement React "
"« exécuter une fois » ; ne pas passer de tableau exécute l'effet à chaque "
"rendu."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:66
msgid ""
"The effect closure runs synchronously inside the component call. Cleanup-on-"
"dep-change (returning a cleanup function) is **not** wired yet — the return "
"value is ignored."
msgstr ""
"La fermeture de l'effet s'exécute de manière synchrone à l'intérieur de "
"l'appel du composant. Le nettoyage lors du changement de dépendance "
"(retourner une fonction de nettoyage) n'est **pas** encore câblé — la valeur "
"de retour est ignorée."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:68
msgid "`useMemo(fn, deps)`"
msgstr "`useMemo(fn, deps)`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:70
msgid ""
"Cache the result of `fn()` keyed by `deps`. Same hash convention as "
"`useEffect`."
msgstr ""
"Met en cache le résultat de `fn()` indexé par `deps`. Même convention de "
"hash que `useEffect`."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:79
msgid ""
"Recomputes on first call or when `deps` change. Otherwise returns the cached "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Recalcule au premier appel ou quand `deps` change. Sinon, retourne la valeur "
"mise en cache."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:81
msgid "`useRef(initial)`"
msgstr "`useRef(initial)`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:83
msgid ""
"A stable mutable cell that doesn't trigger re-renders. Use for values you "
"want to mutate but don't want to drive the UI."
msgstr ""
"Une cellule mutable stable qui ne déclenche pas de re-rendu. À utiliser pour "
"les valeurs que vous souhaitez muter sans piloter l'interface utilisateur."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:85
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const renderCount = useRef(0);\n"
"renderCount.set(renderCount.get() + 1);   // does NOT flip STATE_DIRTY\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const renderCount = useRef(0);\n"
"renderCount.set(renderCount.get() + 1);   // does NOT flip STATE_DIRTY\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:90
msgid ""
"`.get()` reads, `.set(v)` writes. Identity is stable across renders — "
"calling `useRef(0)` at the same position returns the same handle every time, "
"so closures captured in `useEffect` / `useInput` always see the latest value."
msgstr ""
"`.get()` lit, `.set(v)` écrit. L'identité est stable entre les rendus — "
"appeler `useRef(0)` à la même position retourne le même handle à chaque "
"fois, de sorte que les fermetures capturées dans `useEffect` / `useInput` "
"voient toujours la dernière valeur."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:92
msgid ""
"Common pattern: use `useRef` as the canonical buffer for input that gets "
"typed at terminal speed, and pair with a throwaway `useState` to trigger "
"redraws (see the stale-closure gotcha above)."
msgstr ""
"Modèle courant : utiliser `useRef` comme buffer canonique pour les saisies "
"effectuées à la vitesse du terminal, et l'associer à un `useState` jetable "
"pour déclencher les redessinages (voir la mise en garde sur les fermetures "
"périmées ci-dessus)."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:94
msgid "`useApp()`"
msgstr "`useApp()`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:96
msgid "Returns a handle for imperative control of the run loop."
msgstr ""
"Retourne un handle pour le contrôle impératif de la boucle d'exécution."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:98
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const app = useApp();\n"
"// Later:\n"
"app.exit();                    // tells run() to break at the top of the "
"next iteration\n"
"await app.waitUntilExit();     // blocks until EXIT_FLAG is set (rare; "
"usually `run` itself blocks)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const app = useApp();\n"
"// Later:\n"
"app.exit();                    // tells run() to break at the top of the "
"next iteration\n"
"await app.waitUntilExit();     // blocks until EXIT_FLAG is set (rare; "
"usually `run` itself blocks)\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:105
msgid ""
"The handle is stable — calling `useApp()` on every render returns the same "
"singleton. Wrap it in `useRef` if you want to stash it for a callback that "
"outlives the render."
msgstr ""
"Le handle est stable — appeler `useApp()` à chaque rendu retourne le même "
"singleton. Encapsulez-le dans `useRef` si vous souhaitez le conserver pour "
"un callback qui survit au rendu."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:107
msgid "`useStdout()`"
msgstr "`useStdout()`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:109
msgid "Terminal dimensions and a raw-write escape hatch."
msgstr "Dimensions du terminal et échappatoire d'écriture brute."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:111
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const stdout = useStdout();\n"
"const cols = stdout.columns();    // terminal width in cells (falls back to "
"80 if not a TTY)\n"
"const rows = stdout.rows();       // height in cells (fallback 24)\n"
"stdout.write(\"raw bytes\\n\");      // bypass the cell-grid diff\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const stdout = useStdout();\n"
"const cols = stdout.columns();    // terminal width in cells (falls back to "
"80 if not a TTY)\n"
"const rows = stdout.rows();       // height in cells (fallback 24)\n"
"stdout.write(\"raw bytes\\n\");      // bypass the cell-grid diff\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:118
msgid ""
"Use `columns`/`rows` to size dividers, truncate content to fit, or pick a "
"layout direction. `write` is rarely needed — almost everything should go "
"through widgets so the cell-grid diff can render it efficiently."
msgstr ""
"Utilisez `columns`/`rows` pour dimensionner les séparateurs, tronquer le "
"contenu afin qu'il tienne, ou choisir une direction de mise en page. `write` "
"est rarement nécessaire — presque tout devrait passer par les widgets afin "
"que le diff de la grille de cellules puisse le rendre efficacement."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:120
msgid "`useFocus(autoFocus, isActive)`"
msgstr "`useFocus(autoFocus, isActive)`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:122
msgid ""
"Register the calling widget as a focus candidate. Returns `1.0` when this "
"widget is the currently focused one, else `0.0` (treat as truthy/falsy)."
msgstr ""
"Enregistre le widget appelant comme candidat au focus. Retourne `1.0` quand "
"ce widget est celui qui a le focus, sinon `0.0` (traiter comme valeur "
"véridique/falsy)."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:124
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const isFocused = useFocus(1 /* autoFocus */, 1 /* isActive */);\n"
"return Box({ flexDirection: \"row\" }, [\n"
"    Text(\"> \", isFocused ? { color: \"cyan\", bold: true } : { dimColor: "
"true }),\n"
"    Text(\"name input\"),\n"
"]);\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const isFocused = useFocus(1 /* autoFocus */, 1 /* isActive */);\n"
"return Box({ flexDirection: \"row\" }, [\n"
"    Text(\"> \", isFocused ? { color: \"cyan\", bold: true } : { dimColor: "
"true }),\n"
"    Text(\"name input\"),\n"
"]);\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:132
msgid ""
"`autoFocus`: pass `1` for one widget to take focus on first render. "
"Subsequent `useFocus` calls with `autoFocus=1` are ignored once focus has "
"been claimed."
msgstr ""
"`autoFocus` : passer `1` pour qu'un widget prenne le focus au premier rendu. "
"Les appels `useFocus` suivants avec `autoFocus=1` sont ignorés une fois le "
"focus acquis."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:133
msgid ""
"`isActive`: pass `0` to remove this widget from the Tab cycle (e.g. a "
"disabled field)."
msgstr ""
"`isActive` : passer `0` pour retirer ce widget du cycle Tab (ex. un champ "
"désactivé)."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:135
msgid ""
"Tab and Shift-Tab cycle focus automatically — no boilerplate. The run loop's "
"input drain handles the `\\x09` / `\\x1b[Z` byte sequences before forwarding "
"them to your `useInput` handler."
msgstr ""
"Tab et Shift-Tab font circuler le focus automatiquement — sans code "
"répétitif. La boucle d'exécution traite les séquences d'octets `\\x09` / "
"`\\x1b[Z` avant de les transmettre à votre gestionnaire `useInput`."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:137
msgid "For imperative focus control, pair with `useFocusManager()`:"
msgstr ""
"Pour le contrôle impératif du focus, à utiliser avec `useFocusManager()` :"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:139
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const focus = useFocusManager();\n"
"// Later:\n"
"focus.focusNext();\n"
"focus.focusPrevious();\n"
"focus.focus(id);   // by focus id (1-based, in registration order)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const focus = useFocusManager();\n"
"// Later:\n"
"focus.focusNext();\n"
"focus.focusPrevious();\n"
"focus.focus(id);   // by focus id (1-based, in registration order)\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:147 src/tui/hooks.md:178
msgid "`useInput(handler)`"
msgstr "`useInput(handler)`"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:149
msgid ""
"Register a keypress handler. Called once per byte chunk arriving on stdin, "
"in raw mode."
msgstr ""
"Enregistre un gestionnaire de frappe clavier. Appelé une fois par bloc "
"d'octets arrivant sur stdin, en mode brut."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:151
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"useInput((s: string) => {\n"
"    if (s === \"\\x03\") app.exit();               // Ctrl+C\n"
"    if (s === \"\\r\" || s === \"\\n\") onSubmit();   // Enter\n"
"    if (s === \"\\x7f\" || s === \"\\b\") onErase();  // Backspace\n"
"    if (s === \"\\x1b[A\") onUpArrow();            // ANSI up\n"
"    if (s.length === 1 && s >= \" \" && s <= \"~\") onPrintable(s);\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"useInput((s: string) => {\n"
"    if (s === \"\\x03\") app.exit();               // Ctrl+C\n"
"    if (s === \"\\r\" || s === \"\\n\") onSubmit();   // Enter\n"
"    if (s === \"\\x7f\" || s === \"\\b\") onErase();  // Backspace\n"
"    if (s === \"\\x1b[A\") onUpArrow();            // ANSI up\n"
"    if (s.length === 1 && s >= \" \" && s <= \"~\") onPrintable(s);\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:161
msgid ""
"The `s` argument is the raw byte chunk as a string. ANSI escape sequences "
"like arrow keys arrive as a single chunk (`\\x1b[A`, `\\x1b[B`, `\\x1b[C`, "
"`\\x1b[D`); printable characters as one byte; control codes (Ctrl+C, Tab, "
"Enter, Backspace) as their literal byte."
msgstr ""
"L'argument `s` est le bloc d'octets bruts sous forme de chaîne. Les "
"séquences d'échappement ANSI comme les touches directionnelles arrivent en "
"un seul bloc (`\\x1b[A`, `\\x1b[B`, `\\x1b[C`, `\\x1b[D`) ; les caractères "
"imprimables comme un octet ; les codes de contrôle (Ctrl+C, Tab, Entrée, "
"Retour arrière) comme leur octet littéral."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:163
msgid ""
"**Tab handling**: Tab (`\\x09`) and Shift-Tab (`\\x1b[Z`) cycle the focus "
"ring _before_ the handler is called. The handler still sees the byte, so you "
"can branch on it if you want custom Tab behaviour — but for the typical "
"\"Tab moves focus\" case the framework already did it."
msgstr ""
"**Gestion du Tab** : Tab (`\\x09`) et Shift-Tab (`\\x1b[Z`) font avancer le "
"cycle de focus _avant_ l'appel du gestionnaire. Le gestionnaire voit quand "
"même l'octet, vous pouvez donc en tenir compte si vous souhaitez un "
"comportement Tab personnalisé — mais pour le cas typique « Tab déplace le "
"focus », le framework l'a déjà fait."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:165
msgid ""
"Only one handler is registered at a time (last `useInput` call wins). For "
"multiple focusable widgets, dispatch from one handler by checking "
"`useFocus`'s return."
msgstr ""
"Un seul gestionnaire est enregistré à la fois (le dernier appel à `useInput` "
"l'emporte). Pour plusieurs widgets focusables, dispatcher depuis un seul "
"gestionnaire en vérifiant la valeur de retour de `useFocus`."

#: src/tui/hooks.md:167
msgid "Equivalence with ink"
msgstr "Équivalence avec ink"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:169
msgid "ink"
msgstr "ink"

#: src/tui/hooks.md:169 src/api/reference.md:2778
