#: src/platforms/wearos.md:97
msgid ""
"Identical to [Android](android.md) — the same `perry/ui` widgets map to the "
"same Android `View` classes (`Text` → `TextView`, `VStack` → vertical "
"`LinearLayout`, `Button` → `Button`, `ScrollView` → `ScrollView`, and so "
"on). No Wear-specific widget API is required: an Android UI tree renders "
"directly on a watch."
msgstr ""
"Identique à [Android](android.md)  les mêmes widgets `perry/ui` sont mappés "
"aux mêmes classes Android `View` (`Text` → `TextView`, `VStack` → "
"`LinearLayout`, `Button` → `Button`, `ScrollView` → `ScrollView`, et ainsi "
"de suite). Aucune API de widget spécifique à Wear n'est requise: un arbre "
"d'interface utilisateur Android est rendu directement sur une montre."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:102
msgid ""
"The `androidx.wear` dependency in the overlay brings in `BoxInsetLayout` and "
"swipe-to-dismiss so round screens and the back gesture behave like a native "
"Wear app."
msgstr ""
"La dépendance `androidx.wear` dans la superposition apporte `BoxInsetLayout` "
"et le balayage pour rejeter les écrans ronds et le geste arrière se "
"comportent comme une application Wear native."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:108
msgid ""
"A Wear OS app uses the same `App({...})` entry point as every other Perry UI "
"target:"
msgstr ""
"Une application Wear OS utilise le même point d'entrée `App({...})` que "
"toutes les autres cibles d'interface utilisateur Perry:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:111
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { App, Text, VStack, Button, State } from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"\n"
"const count = State(0)\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"My Watch App\",\n"
"    width: 200,\n"
"    height: 200,\n"
"    body: VStack(8, [\n"
"        Text(\"Hello, Wear OS!\"),\n"
"        Text(`Taps: ${count.value}`),\n"
"        Button(\"Tap me\", () => count.set(count.value + 1)),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { App, Text, VStack, Button, State } from \"perry/ui\"\n"
