"The WASM target supports external FFI functions declared with `declare "
"function`. They become WASM imports under the `\"ffi\"` namespace:"
msgstr ""
"La cible WASM prend en charge les fonctions FFI externes déclarées avec "
"`declare function`. Elles deviennent des imports WASM sous l'espace de noms "
"`\"ffi\"` :"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:85
msgid "Provide them when instantiating:"
msgstr "Fournissez-les lors de l'instanciation :"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:88
msgid "// Via __ffiImports global (set before boot)"
msgstr "// Via __ffiImports global (défini avant le démarrage)"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:90
msgid "// Or via bootPerryWasm second argument"
msgstr "// Ou via le deuxième argument bootPerryWasm"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:95
msgid ""
"**Auto-stub for missing imports.** The `ffi` namespace is wrapped in a "
"`Proxy` so any FFI function the host doesn't provide is auto-stubbed with a "
"no-op that returns `TAG_UNDEFINED`. This means apps that use native "
"libraries (e.g. Hone Editor's 56 `hone_editor_*` functions) can still "
"instantiate and run in the browser even without the native bindings — the "
"relevant features are simply no-ops."
msgstr ""
"**Stub automatique pour les imports manquants.** L'espace de noms `ffi` est "
"enveloppé dans un `Proxy` de sorte que toute fonction FFI non fournie par "
"l'hôte est automatiquement remplacée par un no-op renvoyant `TAG_UNDEFINED`. "
"Cela signifie que les applications utilisant des bibliothèques natives (p. "
"ex. les 56 fonctions `hone_editor_*` de Hone Editor) peuvent quand même être "
"instanciées et s'exécuter dans le navigateur même sans les bindings natifs — "
"les fonctionnalités concernées sont simplement des no-ops."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:97
msgid "Module-Level Constants"
msgstr "Constantes de niveau module"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:99
msgid ""
"Top-level `const`/`let` declarations are promoted to dedicated WASM globals "
"so functions in the same module can read them, and so two modules' identical "
"`LocalId`s don't collide:"
msgstr ""
"Les déclarations `const`/`let` de premier niveau sont promues en globals "
"WASM dédiés afin que les fonctions du même module puissent les lire, et que "
"les `LocalId` identiques de deux modules n'entrent pas en collision :"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:101
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// telemetry.ts\n"
"const CHIRP_URL = 'https://api.chirp247.com/api/v1/event'\n"
"const API_KEY   = 'my-key'\n"
"\n"
"export function trackEvent(event: string): void {\n"
"    fetch(CHIRP_URL, {\n"
"        method: 'POST',\n"
"        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Chirp-Key': "
"API_KEY },\n"
"        body: JSON.stringify({ event }),\n"
"    })\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// telemetry.ts\n"
"const CHIRP_URL = 'https://api.chirp247.com/api/v1/event'\n"
"const API_KEY   = 'my-key'\n"
"\n"
"export function trackEvent(event: string): void {\n"
"    fetch(CHIRP_URL, {\n"
"        method: 'POST',\n"
"        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Chirp-Key': "
"API_KEY },\n"
"        body: JSON.stringify({ event }),\n"
"    })\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:115
msgid ""
"Both `CHIRP_URL` and `API_KEY` become WASM globals indexed by `(module_idx, "
"LocalId)`. Reading them from `trackEvent` emits a `global.get` instead of "
"trying to look up a function-local that doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"`CHIRP_URL` et `API_KEY` deviennent tous deux des globals WASM indexés par "
"`(module_idx, LocalId)`. Leur lecture depuis `trackEvent` émet un "
"`global.get` au lieu de tenter de rechercher un local de fonction inexistant."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:117
msgid "JavaScript Runtime Bridge"
msgstr "Pont vers le runtime JavaScript"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:119
msgid ""
"The bridge (`wasm_runtime.js`) is embedded in the HTML and provides ~280 "
"imports across:"
msgstr ""
"Le pont (`wasm_runtime.js`) est intégré dans le HTML et fournit ~280 imports "
"couvrant :"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:121
msgid ""
"**NaN-boxing helpers**: `f64ToU64` / `u64ToF64` / `nanboxString` / "
"`nanboxPointer` / `toJsValue` / `fromJsValue`"
msgstr ""
"**Helpers NaN-boxing** : `f64ToU64` / `u64ToF64` / `nanboxString` / "
"`nanboxPointer` / `toJsValue` / `fromJsValue`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:122
msgid "**String table**: dynamic JS string array indexed by string ID"
msgstr ""
"**Table de chaînes** : tableau de chaînes JS dynamique indexé par "
"identifiant de chaîne"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:123
msgid ""
"**Handle store**: maps integer handle IDs to JS objects, arrays, closures, "
"promises, DOM elements"
msgstr ""
"**Store de handles** : associe des identifiants de handle entiers à des "
"objets JS, tableaux, closures, promises, éléments DOM"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:124
msgid ""
"**Core ops**: console, math, JSON, JSON.parse/stringify, Date, RegExp, URL, "
"Map, Set, Buffer, fetch"
msgstr ""
"**Opérations de base** : console, math, JSON, JSON.parse/stringify, Date, "
"RegExp, URL, Map, Set, Buffer, fetch"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:125
msgid ""
"**Closure dispatch**: indirect function table + capture array, with "
"`closure_call_0/1/2/3/spread`"
msgstr ""
"**Dispatch de closures** : table de fonctions indirectes + tableau de "
"captures, avec `closure_call_0/1/2/3/spread`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:126
msgid ""
"**Class dispatch**: `class_new`, `class_call_method`, `class_get_field`, "
"`class_set_field`, parent table for inheritance"
msgstr ""
"**Dispatch de classes** : `class_new`, `class_call_method`, "
"`class_get_field`, `class_set_field`, table parente pour l'héritage"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:127
msgid ""
"**DOM widgets**: 168+ `perry_ui_*` functions covering every widget in `perry/"
"ui`"
msgstr ""
"**Widgets DOM** : 168+ fonctions `perry_ui_*` couvrant chaque widget de "
"`perry/ui`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:128
msgid ""
"**Async functions**: compiled to JS function bodies and merged into the "
"import object as `__async_<name>`"
msgstr ""
"**Fonctions async** : compilées en corps de fonctions JS et fusionnées dans "
"l'objet d'import sous la forme `__async_<name>`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:130
msgid ""
"All host imports are wrapped via `wrapImportsForI64()` so they automatically "
"reinterpret BigInt args (from WASM i64 params) into f64 internally and "
"reinterpret Number returns back into BigInt. Without this wrapping, every "
"NaN-valued f64 return would crash with \"Cannot convert NaN to a BigInt\"."
msgstr ""
"Tous les imports hôtes sont enveloppés via `wrapImportsForI64()` afin de "
"réinterpréter automatiquement les arguments BigInt (provenant des paramètres "
"i64 WASM) en f64 en interne et de réinterpréter les valeurs de retour Number "
"en BigInt. Sans cet enveloppement, chaque retour f64 à valeur NaN planterait "
"avec \"Cannot convert NaN to a BigInt\"."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:132
msgid "Web Worker Threading"
msgstr "Threading avec Web Workers"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:134
msgid "`perry/thread` works in the browser via a Web Worker pool:"
msgstr ""
"`perry/thread` fonctionne dans le navigateur via un pool de Web Workers :"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:144
msgid ""
"Each worker instantiates its own WASM module with the same bytecode and "
"bridge. Values cross between the main thread and workers via structured-"
"clone serialization. See [Threading](../threading/overview.md)."
msgstr ""
"Chaque worker instancie son propre module WASM avec le même bytecode et le "
"même pont. Les valeurs transitent entre le thread principal et les workers "
"via la sérialisation structured-clone. Voir [Threading](../threading/"
"overview.md)."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:148
msgid ""
"**No file system access** beyond the File System Access API "
"(`window.showDirectoryPicker()`)"
msgstr ""
"**Pas d'accès au système de fichiers** au-delà de la File System Access API "
"(`window.showDirectoryPicker()`)"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:149
msgid "**No raw TCP/UDP sockets** — only `fetch()` and `WebSocket`"
msgstr "**Pas de sockets TCP/UDP bruts** — uniquement `fetch()` et `WebSocket`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:150
msgid "**No subprocess spawning** — `child_process.exec` etc. are no-ops"
msgstr ""
"**Pas de création de sous-processus** — `child_process.exec` et autres sont "
"des no-ops"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:151
msgid ""
"**No native databases** — SQLite, Postgres, MySQL drivers don't compile to "
"web"
msgstr ""
"**Pas de bases de données natives** — les drivers SQLite, Postgres, MySQL ne "
"compilent pas pour le web"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:152
msgid ""
"**CORS** applies to all `fetch()` calls — third-party APIs must allow your "
"origin"
msgstr ""
"**CORS** s'applique à tous les appels `fetch()` — les APIs tierces doivent "
"autoriser votre origine"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:153
msgid ""
"**localStorage**, not real keychain — fine for preferences, not for secrets"
msgstr ""
"**localStorage**, et non un vrai keychain — convient aux préférences, pas "
"aux secrets"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:154
msgid ""
"Source-mapped stack traces are JS-only; WASM stack frames show `wasm-"
"function[N]`"
msgstr ""
"Les traces de pile avec sourcemap sont uniquement JS ; les frames WASM "
"affichent `wasm-function[N]`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:156
msgid "Minification"
msgstr "Minification"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:158
msgid ""
"Use `--minify` to minify the embedded JS runtime bridge in the HTML output. "
"The Rust-native JS minifier strips comments, collapses whitespace, and "
"mangles internal identifiers, compressing the runtime from ~3,400 lines to "
"~180."
msgstr ""
"Utilisez `--minify` pour minifier le pont JS du runtime intégré dans le HTML "
"de sortie. Le minifieur JS natif Rust supprime les commentaires, compresse "
"les espaces blancs et modifie les identifiants internes, réduisant le "
"runtime de ~3 400 lignes à ~180."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:164
msgid "Example: Counter App"
msgstr "Exemple : Application Compteur"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:187
msgid "Example: Real-World App (Mango MongoDB GUI)"
msgstr "Exemple : Application réelle (Mango, interface graphique MongoDB)"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:189
msgid ""
"The [Mango](https://github.com/MangoQuery/app) MongoDB GUI — 50 modules, 998 "
"functions, classes, async functions, fetch with custom headers, the Hone "
"code editor — compiles to a single 4 MB HTML file via `--target web` and "
"renders its full UI (welcome screen, query view, edit view) in the browser. "
"SQLite-backed connection storage gracefully degrades to an in-memory "
"transient store on web; the rest of the app works the same as the native "
"version."
msgstr ""
"L'interface utilisateur graphique [Mango](https://github.com/MangoQuery/app) "
"MongoDB  50 modules, 998 fonctions, classes, fonctions asynchrones, "
"récupération avec en-têtes personnalisés, l'éditeur de code Hone  compile en "
"un seul fichier HTML de 4 Mo via `--target web` et affiche son interface "
"utilisateur complète (écran de bienvenue, vue de requête, vue d'édition) "
"dans le navigateur. Le stockage de connexion soutenu par SQLite se dégrade "
"gracieusement en un stockage transitoire en mémoire sur le Web; le reste de "
"l'application fonctionne de la même manière que la version native."

