"    console.log(cache.get(\"key\"))   // \"value\"\n"
"    console.log(cache.has(\"key\"))   // true\n"
"    cache.delete(\"key\")\n"
"    cache.clear()\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/other.md:291
msgid "child_process"
msgstr "child_process"

#: src/stdlib/other.md:293
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"// `spawnBackground` / `getProcessStatus` / `killProcess` are Perry "
"EXTENSIONS —\n"
"// Node's `child_process` has no such named exports, so importing them by "
"name\n"
"// is rejected (correctly) with U006. Reach them through the module "
"namespace.\n"
"import * as child_process from \"child_process\"\n"
"\n"
"function childProcessExample(): void {\n"
"    // Spawn a background process\n"
"    const { pid, handleId } = child_process.spawnBackground(\"sleep\", "
"[\"10\"], \"/tmp/log.txt\")\n"
"\n"
"    // Check if it's still running\n"
"    const status = child_process.getProcessStatus(handleId)\n"
"    console.log(status.alive) // true\n"
"    console.log(`pid=${pid}`)\n"
"\n"
"    // Kill it\n"
"    child_process.killProcess(handleId)\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"// `spawnBackground` / `getProcessStatus` / `killProcess` are Perry "
"EXTENSIONS —\n"
"// Node's `child_process` has no such named exports, so importing them by "
"name\n"
"// is rejected (correctly) with U006. Reach them through the module "
"namespace.\n"
"import * as child_process from \"child_process\"\n"
"\n"
"function childProcessExample(): void {\n"
"    // Spawn a background process\n"
"    const { pid, handleId } = child_process.spawnBackground(\"sleep\", "
"[\"10\"], \"/tmp/log.txt\")\n"
"\n"
"    // Check if it's still running\n"
"    const status = child_process.getProcessStatus(handleId)\n"
"    console.log(status.alive) // true\n"
"    console.log(`pid=${pid}`)\n"
"\n"
"    // Kill it\n"
"    child_process.killProcess(handleId)\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/other.md:313
msgid "node-pty (Pseudo-terminals)"
msgstr "node-pty (Pseudo-terminals)"

#: src/stdlib/other.md:315
msgid ""
"A runtime-native pty (#6563) — `openpty`/`fork` with the slave as the "
"child's controlling terminal, no N-API addon. Importable as both `node-pty` "
"and the API-identical `@lydell/node-pty` fork, statically or via dynamic "
"`import()`. POSIX only for now (macOS + Linux); on other hosts `spawn` "
"throws, which triggers consumers' non-pty fallback paths."
msgstr ""
"Une pty native en temps d'exécution (#6563)  `openpty`/`fork` avec l'esclave "
"comme terminal de contrôle de l'enfant, sans addon N-API. Importé à la fois "
"sous la forme de `node-pty` et de la fourchette `@lydell/node-pty` identique "
"à l'API, de manière statique ou via `import()` dynamique. POSIX seulement "
"pour le moment (macOS + Linux); sur d'autres hôtes `spawn` lance, ce qui "
"déclenche les chemins de secours non vides des consommateurs."

#: src/stdlib/other.md:321
msgid ""
"`onData` delivers UTF-8 strings (multi-byte sequences split across reads are "
"reassembled); `onExit` fires `{ exitCode, signal }` with the numeric signal "
"for a signal death and `undefined` otherwise; `kill()` defaults to `SIGHUP` "
"like node-pty. `TERM` in the child comes from `name`."
msgstr ""
"`onData` fournit des chaînes UTF-8 (les séquences de plusieurs octets "
"réparties sur les lectures sont réassemblées); `onExit` déclenche "
"`{ exitCode, signal }` avec le signal numérique pour une mort du signal et "
"`undefined` autrement; `kill()` par défaut à `SIGHUP` comme node-pty. Le "
"`TERM` chez l'enfant provient du `name`."

#: src/stdlib/other.md:326
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import { spawn } from \"node-pty\";\n"
"\n"
"const term = spawn(\"bash\", [], {\n"
"  name: \"xterm-256color\",\n"
"  cols: 80,\n"
"  rows: 24,\n"
"  cwd: process.cwd(),\n"
"  env: process.env,\n"
"});\n"
"\n"
"const sub = term.onData((data) => process.stdout.write(data));\n"
"term.onExit(({ exitCode, signal }) => {\n"
"  console.log(`exited: code=${exitCode} signal=${signal ?? \"none\"}`);\n"
"});\n"
"\n"
"term.write(\"echo hello\\n\");\n"
"term.resize(120, 40);   // TIOCSWINSZ → child sees SIGWINCH\n"
"term.kill(\"SIGTERM\");   // no argument = SIGHUP\n"
"sub.dispose();          // unsubscribe onData\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import { spawn } from \"node-pty\";\n"
"\n"
"const term = spawn(\"bash\", [], {\n"
"  name: \"xterm-256color\",\n"
"  cols: 80,\n"
"  rows: 24,\n"
"  cwd: process.cwd(),\n"
"  env: process.env,\n"
"});\n"
"\n"
"const sub = term.onData((data) => process.stdout.write(data));\n"
"term.onExit(({ exitCode, signal }) => {\n"
"  console.log(`exited: code=${exitCode} signal=${signal ?? \"none\"}`);\n"
"});\n"
"\n"
"term.write(\"echo hello\\n\");\n"
"term.resize(120, 40);   // TIOCSWINSZ → child sees SIGWINCH\n"
"term.kill(\"SIGTERM\");   // no argument = SIGHUP\n"
"sub.dispose();          // unsubscribe onData\n"
"```"

#: src/stdlib/other.md:348
msgid "@parcel/watcher"
msgstr "@parcel/watcher"

#: src/stdlib/other.md:350
msgid ""
"Perry provides the low-level `@parcel/watcher` binding object and all eight "
"published platform-package names through one `notify`\\-backed native "
"facade. The pure-JavaScript `@parcel/watcher/wrapper` continues to compile "
"normally; its target-dependent platform `require` is folded to the native "
"facade at compile time. The behavior was checked against `@parcel/watcher` "
"2.5.1."
msgstr ""
"Perry fournit l'objet de liaison `@parcel/watcher` de bas niveau et les huit "
"noms de plate-forme publiés à travers une façade native `notify`\\-backed. "
"Le pur-JavaScript `@parcel/watcher/wrapper` continue à compiler normalement; "
"sa plate-forme dépendante de la cible `require` est pliée à la façade native "
"au moment de la compilation. Le comportement a été vérifié par `@parcel/"
"watcher` 2.5.1."

#: src/stdlib/other.md:356
msgid ""
"Subscriptions use FSEvents on macOS, inotify on Linux, ReadDirectoryChangesW "
"on Windows, and notify's native backend on other supported systems. An "
"unknown or unavailable requested backend falls back to the platform default. "
"Events are delivered on Perry's main thread in coalesced batches: create "
"followed by update remains one `create`, create followed by delete "
"disappears, and rename is `delete` for the old path plus `create` for the "
"new path. Backend overflow/rescan notifications trigger a fresh tree "
"snapshot and emit its diff."
msgstr ""
"Les abonnements utilisent FSEvents sur macOS, notify sur Linux, "
"ReadDirectoryChangesW sur Windows et notify's native backend sur les autres "
"systèmes pris en charge. Un back-end demandé inconnu ou indisponible revient "
"à la plate-forme par défaut. Les événements sont livrés sur le fil principal "
"de Perry en lots fusionnés: la création suivie de la mise à jour reste un "
"`create`, la création suivie de la suppression disparaît et le renom est "
"`delete` pour l'ancien chemin plus `create` pour le nouveau chemin. Les "
"notifications overflow/rescan du backend déclenchent un nouvel instantané "
"d'arbre et émettent sa différence."

#: src/stdlib/other.md:365
msgid ""
"`ignorePaths` are absolute path prefixes. `ignoreGlobs` are the regex "
"sources produced by the package's JS wrapper and match root-relative paths, "
"including dot-files. `unsubscribe` matches directory, callback identity, and "
"normalized options; it stops the native watcher and drains queued events "
"before its promise resolves, so no callback fires afterward. Live "
"subscriptions keep the event loop active. `writeSnapshot` and "
"`getEventsSince` use the same snapshot diff semantics as overflow recovery."
msgstr ""
"`ignorePaths` sont des préfixes de chemin absolu. `ignoreGlobs` sont les "
"sources de régex produites par l'emballage JS du package et correspondent "
"aux chemins relatifs à la racine, y compris les fichiers en points. "
"`unsubscribe` correspond au répertoire, à l'identité de rappel et aux "
"options normalisées; il arrête l'observateur natif et évacue les événements "
"en file d'attente avant la résolution de sa promesse, de sorte qu'aucun "
"rappel ne se déclenche par la suite. Les abonnements en direct maintiennent "
"la boucle d'événement active. `writeSnapshot` et `getEventsSince` utilisent "
"la même sémantique de différence d'instantané que la récupération de "
"débordement."

