"`down()`."

#: src/container/compose.md:364
msgid ""
"[Production patterns](./production-patterns.md) — case study with the "
"Forgejo example."
msgstr ""
"[Patterns de production](./production-patterns.md) — étude de cas avec "
"l'exemple Forgejo."

#: src/container/compose.md:366
msgid ""
"[Security](./security.md) — image verification and capability isolation."
msgstr ""
"[Sécurité](./security.md) — vérification des images et isolation des "
"capacités."

#: src/container/networking.md:3
msgid ""
"Compose stacks join one or more user-defined networks. Each container spec "
"lists the networks it joins; the engine creates the networks (if they don't "
"already exist) before starting any service. This page covers the day-to-day "
"networking patterns Perry users hit."
msgstr ""
"Les stacks Compose rejoignent un ou plusieurs réseaux définis par "
"l'utilisateur. Chaque spec de conteneur liste les réseaux qu'il rejoint ; le "
"moteur crée les réseaux (s'ils n'existent pas déjà) avant de démarrer tout "
"service. Cette page couvre les patterns réseau courants rencontrés par les "
"utilisateurs de Perry."

#: src/container/networking.md:8
msgid "Defining networks"
msgstr "Définition des réseaux"

#: src/container/networking.md:10
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const stack = await up({\n"
"  version: \"3.8\",\n"
"  services: {\n"
"    api: { image: \"myapp/api\", networks: [\"app-net\"] },\n"
"    db:  { image: \"postgres:16-alpine\", networks: [\"app-net\"] },\n"
"  },\n"
"  networks: {\n"
"    \"app-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },\n"
"  },\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"const stack = await up({\n"
"  version: \"3.8\",\n"
"  services: {\n"
"    api: { image: \"myapp/api\", networks: [\"app-net\"] },\n"
"    db:  { image: \"postgres:16-alpine\", networks: [\"app-net\"] },\n"
"  },\n"
"  networks: {\n"
"    \"app-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },\n"
"  },\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/container/networking.md:23
msgid "Recognised `ComposeNetwork` fields:"
msgstr "Champs `ComposeNetwork` reconnus :"

#: src/container/networking.md:27 src/container/volumes.md:39
msgid "`driver`"
msgstr "`driver`"

#: src/container/networking.md:27
msgid "Network driver (`\"bridge\"` is the default; `\"overlay\"` for swarm)."
msgstr ""
"Driver réseau (`\"bridge\"` est la valeur par défaut ; `\"overlay\"` pour "
"swarm)."

#: src/container/networking.md:28 src/container/volumes.md:40
msgid "`external`"
msgstr "`external`"

#: src/container/networking.md:28
msgid "Don't create — assume the network already exists."
msgstr "Ne pas créer — suppose que le réseau existe déjà."

#: src/container/networking.md:29
msgid "Override the network's runtime name."
msgstr "Remplace le nom runtime du réseau."

#: src/container/networking.md:30
msgid "`internal`"
msgstr "`internal`"

#: src/container/networking.md:30
msgid ""
"**Internal-only**: containers attached have no external bridge or routing. "
"See below."
msgstr ""
"**Interne uniquement** : les conteneurs connectés n'ont pas de bridge "
"externe ni de routage. Voir ci-dessous."

#: src/container/networking.md:31
msgid "`driver_opts`"
msgstr "`driver_opts`"

#: src/container/networking.md:31
msgid "Driver-specific options."
msgstr "Options spécifiques au driver."

#: src/container/networking.md:32
msgid "Network labels."
msgstr "Labels réseau."

#: src/container/networking.md:34
msgid "Internal-only networks (`internal: true`)"
msgstr "Réseaux internes uniquement (`internal: true`)"

#: src/container/networking.md:36
msgid ""
"A network with `internal: true` blocks egress to anything outside the "
"network. Containers on it can talk to each other, but **cannot reach the "
"host or the public internet**, and the host cannot reach them via published "
"ports. This is the canonical \"private database side-channel\" pattern:"
msgstr ""
"Un réseau avec `internal: true` bloque l'egress vers tout ce qui est en "
"dehors du réseau. Les conteneurs qui y sont attachés peuvent communiquer "
"entre eux, mais **ne peuvent pas atteindre l'hôte ni l'internet public**, et "
"l'hôte ne peut pas les atteindre via des ports publiés. C'est le pattern "
"canonique de « canal latéral base de données privée » :"

#: src/container/networking.md:42
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"networks: {\n"
"  \"app-db-net\":  { driver: \"bridge\", internal: true },  // db <-> api "
"only\n"
"  \"app-web-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },                  // api <-> host\n"
"},\n"
"services: {\n"
"  db: {\n"
"    image: \"postgres:16-alpine\",\n"
"    networks: [\"app-db-net\"],   // db is reachable ONLY from app-db-net\n"
"    // no `ports:` — postgres is unpublished\n"
"  },\n"
"  api: {\n"
"    image: \"myapp/api\",\n"
"    networks: [\"app-db-net\", \"app-web-net\"],\n"
"    ports: [\"8080:8080\"],       // api published on the host\n"
"  },\n"
"},\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"networks: {\n"
"  \"app-db-net\":  { driver: \"bridge\", internal: true },  // db <-> api "
"only\n"
"  \"app-web-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" },                  // api <-> host\n"
"},\n"
"services: {\n"
"  db: {\n"
"    image: \"postgres:16-alpine\",\n"
"    networks: [\"app-db-net\"],   // db is reachable ONLY from app-db-net\n"
"    // no `ports:` — postgres is unpublished\n"
"  },\n"
"  api: {\n"
"    image: \"myapp/api\",\n"
"    networks: [\"app-db-net\", \"app-web-net\"],\n"
"    ports: [\"8080:8080\"],       // api published on the host\n"
"  },\n"
"},\n"
"```"

#: src/container/networking.md:61
msgid ""
"The api container straddles both networks: it can reach `db` over `app-db-"
"net` and accept inbound HTTP from the host on `app-web-net`. postgres is "
"invisible to anything not on `app-db-net`."
msgstr ""
"Le conteneur api chevauche les deux réseaux : il peut atteindre `db` via "
"`app-db-net` et accepter du trafic HTTP entrant de l'hôte sur `app-web-net`. "
"postgres est invisible pour tout ce qui n'est pas sur `app-db-net`."

#: src/container/networking.md:67
msgid ""
"Within a user-defined bridge network, the backend's embedded DNS resolves "
"container names and registered aliases to IP addresses. Perry registers each "
"compose service key (`db`, `api`, …) as a network alias on Docker, Podman, "
"and Lima, so sibling services can use ordinary compose-style hostnames:"
msgstr ""
"Dans un réseau de pont défini par l'utilisateur, le DNS intégré du back-end "
"résout les noms de conteneurs et les alias enregistrés aux adresses IP. "
"Perry enregistre chaque clé de service de composition (`db`, `api`, ...) "
"comme un alias réseau sur Docker, Podman et Lima, de sorte que les services "
"frères et sœurs peuvent utiliser des noms d'hôte ordinaires de style "
"composition:"

#: src/container/networking.md:72
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"api: {\n"
"  image: \"myapp/api\",\n"
"  environment: {\n"
"    DATABASE_URL: \"postgres://user:pw@db:5432/app\",\n"
"  },\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"api: {\n"
"  image: \"myapp/api\",\n"
"  environment: {\n"
"    DATABASE_URL: \"postgres://user:pw@db:5432/app\",\n"
"  },\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/container/networking.md:81
msgid ""
"`apple/container` does not expose network aliases. Perry therefore drops "
"this capability with an explicit warning (or rejects the compose plan in "
"strict enforcement mode). For portable service discovery that must also work "
"with the Apple backend, set `container_name` explicitly and use that name in "
"sibling URLs:"
msgstr ""
"`apple/container` n'expose pas les alias du réseau. Perry supprime donc "
"cette fonctionnalité avec un avertissement explicite (ou rejette le plan de "
"composition en mode strict d'exécution). Pour la découverte de service "
"portable qui doit également fonctionner avec le back-end Apple, définissez "
"`container_name` explicitement et utilisez ce nom dans les URL frères:"

#: src/container/networking.md:87
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// IMPORTANT: Perry's compose engine creates each container with a\n"
"// `{md5}-{random_hex}` derived name and DOES NOT (yet) register the\n"
"// service KEY (`db`, `api`, …) as a network alias. So\n"
"// `DATABASE_URL: 'postgres://user:pw@db:5432/app'` would fail name\n"
"// resolution at runtime. Two ways to make sibling-DNS work:\n"
"//\n"
"//   (a) Set `container_name` explicitly on each service so the\n"
"//       chosen name is what Docker's embedded DNS resolves. This is\n"
"//       the simplest pattern and is what the Forgejo example uses.\n"
"//\n"
"//   (b) Wait for service-key network-alias support (planned).\n"
"//\n"
"// Until (b) lands, prefer (a):\n"
"import { up as upDns } from \"perry/compose\";\n"
"\n"
"async function dnsAwareStack(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    await upDns({\n"
"        version: \"3.8\",\n"
"        services: {\n"
"            db: {\n"
"                image: \"postgres:16-alpine\",\n"
"                container_name: \"myapp-db\", // ← stable DNS target\n"
"                networks: [\"myapp-net\"],\n"
"                environment: { POSTGRES_PASSWORD: \"x\" },\n"
"            },\n"
"            api: {\n"
"                image: \"myapp/api\",\n"
"                container_name: \"myapp-api\",\n"
"                networks: [\"myapp-net\"],\n"
"                environment: {\n"
"                    // Use the container_name as the hostname:\n"
"                    DATABASE_URL: \"postgres://postgres:x@myapp-db:5432/"
"postgres\",\n"
"                },\n"
"            },\n"
"        },\n"
"        networks: { \"myapp-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" } },\n"
"    });\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// IMPORTANT: Perry's compose engine creates each container with a\n"
"// `{md5}-{random_hex}` derived name and DOES NOT (yet) register the\n"
"// service KEY (`db`, `api`, …) as a network alias. So\n"
"// `DATABASE_URL: 'postgres://user:pw@db:5432/app'` would fail name\n"
"// resolution at runtime. Two ways to make sibling-DNS work:\n"
"//\n"
"//   (a) Set `container_name` explicitly on each service so the\n"
"//       chosen name is what Docker's embedded DNS resolves. This is\n"
"//       the simplest pattern and is what the Forgejo example uses.\n"
"//\n"
"//   (b) Wait for service-key network-alias support (planned).\n"
"//\n"
"// Until (b) lands, prefer (a):\n"
"import { up as upDns } from \"perry/compose\";\n"
"\n"
"async function dnsAwareStack(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    await upDns({\n"
"        version: \"3.8\",\n"
"        services: {\n"
"            db: {\n"
"                image: \"postgres:16-alpine\",\n"
"                container_name: \"myapp-db\", // ← stable DNS target\n"
"                networks: [\"myapp-net\"],\n"
"                environment: { POSTGRES_PASSWORD: \"x\" },\n"
"            },\n"
"            api: {\n"
"                image: \"myapp/api\",\n"
"                container_name: \"myapp-api\",\n"
"                networks: [\"myapp-net\"],\n"
"                environment: {\n"
"                    // Use the container_name as the hostname:\n"
"                    DATABASE_URL: \"postgres://postgres:x@myapp-db:5432/"
"postgres\",\n"
"                },\n"
"            },\n"
"        },\n"
"        networks: { \"myapp-net\": { driver: \"bridge\" } },\n"
"    });\n"
"}\n"
"```"

