#: src/widgets/overview.md:3
msgid ""
"Perry can compile TypeScript widget declarations to native widget extensions "
"across 4 platforms: iOS (WidgetKit), Android (App Widgets), watchOS "
"(Complications), and Wear OS (Tiles)."
msgstr ""
"Perry peut compiler des déclarations de widgets TypeScript en extensions de "
"widgets natifs sur 4 plateformes : iOS (WidgetKit), Android (App Widgets), "
"watchOS (Complications) et Wear OS (Tiles)."

#: src/widgets/overview.md:5
msgid ""
"**Status:** the `perry/widget` API is wired in the HIR (`crates/perry-hir/"
"src/lower.rs:try_lower_widget_decl`) and emits via dedicated codegen crates "
"(`perry-codegen-glance`, `perry-codegen-wear-tiles`, the WidgetKit emitter). "
"The snippets on the widget docs pages compile-link cleanly on the host LLVM "
"target — `Widget({...})` lowers to a no-op there — and CI verifies that via "
"[`docs/examples/widgets/snippets.ts`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/blob/"
"main/docs/examples/widgets/snippets.ts). The doc-tests harness accepts a `// "
"widget-bundle-id:` banner and passes it through as `--app-bundle-id`; that "
"plumbing closed [\\#194](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/194). The "
"shared snippets on these pages currently exercise the host compile/link "
"path, while `_smoketest_bundleid.ts` exercises the banner. A target is "
"compiled end-to-end only on a CI host where its Xcode or Android SDK is "
"available. For a working end-to-end reference see [`examples/widget_demo.ts`]"
"(https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/blob/main/examples/widget_demo.ts)."
msgstr ""
"**Le statut:** l'API `perry/widget` est câblée dans le HIR (`crates/perry-"
"hir/src/lower.rs:try_lower_widget_decl`) et émet via des caisses de code "
"génétique dédiées (`perry-codegen-glance`, `perry-codegen-wear-tiles`, "
"l'émetteur WidgetKit). Les extraits sur les pages de widget docs compilent-"
"lient proprement sur l'hôte LLVM cible  `Widget({...})` diminue à un no-op "
"là  et CI vérifie cela via [`docs/examples/widgets/snippets.ts`](https://"
"github.com/PerryTS/perry/blob/main/docs/examples/widgets/snippets.ts). Le "
"harnais doc-tests accepte une bannière `// widget-bundle-id:` et la passe "
"comme `--app-bundle-id`; cette plomberie a fermé [\\#194](https://github.com/"
"PerryTS/perry/issues/194). Les extraits partagés sur ces pages utilisent "
"actuellement le chemin compile/link, tandis que `_smoketest_bundleid.ts` "
"utilise la bannière. Une cible est compilée de bout en bout uniquement sur "
"un hôte CI dont le SDK Xcode ou Android est disponible. Pour une référence "
"de bout en bout, voir [`examples/widget_demo.ts`](https://github.com/PerryTS/"
"perry/blob/main/examples/widget_demo.ts)."

#: src/widgets/overview.md:19
msgid "What Are Widgets?"
msgstr "Que sont les Widgets ?"

#: src/widgets/overview.md:21
msgid ""
"Home screen widgets display glanceable information outside your app. Perry's "
"`perry/widget` module lets you define widgets in TypeScript that compile to "
"each platform's native widget system."
msgstr ""
"Les widgets de l'écran d'accueil affichent des informations consultables en "
"dehors de votre application. Le module `perry/widget` de Perry vous permet "
"de définir des widgets en TypeScript qui compilent vers le système de "
"widgets natif de chaque plateforme."

#: src/widgets/overview.md:23
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"Widget({\n"
"    kind: \"MyWidget\",\n"
"    displayName: \"My Widget\",\n"
"    description: \"Shows a greeting\",\n"
"    entryFields: { name: \"string\" },\n"
"    render: (entry) =>\n"
"        VStack([\n"
"            Text(`Hello, ${entry.name}!`),\n"
"        ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
