#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:109
msgid ""
"**Setup requirement (iOS):** Add an App Group capability in Xcode to both "
"the main app target and the widget extension target. The identifier must "
"match the `appGroup` value."
msgstr ""
"**Prérequis de configuration (iOS) :** Ajoutez une capacité App Group dans "
"Xcode à la fois pour la cible de l'application principale et pour la cible "
"de l'extension de widget. L'identifiant doit correspondre à la valeur "
"`appGroup`."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:111
msgid "Android / Wear OS: SharedPreferences"
msgstr "Android / Wear OS : SharedPreferences"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:113
msgid ""
"On Android, shared storage maps to `SharedPreferences` with the name "
"`perry_shared`. The generated `Bridge.kt` reads values via "
"`context.getSharedPreferences(\"perry_shared\", MODE_PRIVATE)`."
msgstr ""
"Sur Android, le stockage partagé est associé à `SharedPreferences` avec le "
"nom `perry_shared`. Le fichier `Bridge.kt` généré lit les valeurs via "
"`context.getSharedPreferences(\"perry_shared\", MODE_PRIVATE)`."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:115
msgid "Reload Policies"
msgstr "Politiques de rechargement"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:117
msgid ""
"The `reloadPolicy` field controls when the system next calls your provider:"
msgstr ""
"Le champ `reloadPolicy` contrôle quand le système appelle à nouveau votre "
"provider :"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:126
msgid ""
"The refresh interval is read **at compile time**: the compiler scans the "
"provider's `return` statements for a literal `reloadPolicy: { after: "
"{ minutes: N } }` (where `N` is a numeric literal; fractional values round "
"to the nearest second) and bakes the interval into the generated platform "
"code. A `reloadPolicy` computed at runtime (a variable, a function call, …) "
"cannot be read — the compiler warns and the platform default applies."
msgstr ""
"L'intervalle de mise à jour est lu **à la compilation**: le compilateur "
"scanne les instructions `return` du fournisseur pour un `reloadPolicy: "
"{ after: { minutes: N } }` littéral (où `N` est un littéral numérique; les "
"valeurs fractionnaires arrondis à la seconde la plus proche) et cuit "
"l'intervalle dans le code de la plateforme généré. Un `reloadPolicy` calculé "
"à l'exécution (une variable, un appel de fonction, ...) ne peut pas être lu  "
"le compilateur prévient et la plate-forme par défaut s'applique."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:136
msgid "`{ after: { minutes: N } }`"
msgstr "`{ after: { minutes: N } }`"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:136
msgid ""
"Re-fetch after N minutes. Compiles to "
"`.after(Date().addingTimeInterval(N*60))` on iOS/watchOS, "
"`android:updatePeriodMillis=\"N*60000\"` on Android, and "
"`setFreshnessIntervalMillis(N*60000)` on Wear OS."
msgstr ""
"Retour après N minutes. Compile à `.after(Date().addingTimeInterval(N*60))` "
"sur iOS/watchOS, `android:updatePeriodMillis=\"N*60000\"` sur Android et "
"`setFreshnessIntervalMillis(N*60000)` sur le système d'exploitation Wear."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:137
msgid "_(omitted)_"
msgstr "_(omis)_"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:137
msgid ""
"Platform default: 30 minutes on iOS/watchOS, 30 minutes on Android, 60 "
"minutes on Wear OS."
msgstr ""
"Plateforme par défaut: 30 minutes sur iOS/watchOS, 30 minutes sur Android, "
"60 minutes sur Wear OS."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:139
msgid ""
"**Platform floors:** each platform ignores refresh requests below a minimum "
"interval, so the compiler clamps and warns:"
msgstr ""
"**Planchers de plateforme:** Chaque plateforme ignore les demandes de "
"rafraîchissement inférieures à un intervalle minimum, donc le compilateur "
"s'accroche et prévient:"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:142
msgid "Minimum (clamped)"
msgstr "Minimum (clampé)"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:144
msgid "iOS / watchOS (WidgetKit)"
msgstr "iOS / watchOS (WidgetKit)"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:144 src/widgets/data-fetching.md:145
msgid "30 minutes"
msgstr "30 minutes"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:144
msgid "15 minutes (refresh budget)"
msgstr "15 minutes (renouvellement du budget)"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:145
msgid "Android (Glance, `updatePeriodMillis`)"
msgstr "Android (en un coup d'œil, `updatePeriodMillis`)"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:145
msgid "30 minutes (hard framework floor)"
msgstr "30 minutes (plancher à cadre rigide)"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:146
msgid "Wear OS (Tiles freshness)"
msgstr "Wear OS (fraîcheur des carreaux)"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:146
msgid "60 minutes"
msgstr "60 minutes"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:146
msgid "15 minutes"
msgstr "15 minutes"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:148
msgid ""
"If different `return` statements carry different literal policies (e.g. a "
"short error-retry interval and a longer happy-path one), the smallest one "
"wins — the interval is a single compile-time constant per widget — and the "
"compiler emits a warning naming the value it chose."
msgstr ""
"Si différentes instructions `return` comportent des politiques littérales "
"différentes (e.g. un intervalle court de tentative d'erreur et un intervalle "
"plus long de chemin heureux), le plus petit gagne  l'intervalle est une "
"seule constante de temps de compilation par widget  et le compilateur émet "
"un avertissement nommant la valeur qu'il a choisie."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:153
msgid ""
"**Budget limits:** iOS restricts widget refreshes. Typical budget is 40--70 "
"refreshes per day. watchOS is stricter (see [watchOS Complications]"
"(watchos.md)). Request only what you need."
msgstr ""
"**Limites de budget :** iOS restreint les actualisations des widgets. Le "
"budget typique est de 40 à 70 actualisations par jour. watchOS est plus "
"strict (voir [Complications watchOS](watchos.md)). Ne demandez que ce dont "
"vous avez besoin."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:155
msgid "JSON Response Handling"
msgstr "Traitement des réponses JSON"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:157
msgid ""
"The provider function receives the parsed JSON directly. Entry field types "
"must match your `entryFields` declaration:"
msgstr ""
"La fonction provider reçoit directement le JSON parsé. Les types des champs "
"d'entrée doivent correspondre à votre déclaration `entryFields` :"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:159
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"entryFields: {\n"
"  items: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"object\", fields: { name: "
"\"string\", count: \"number\" } } },\n"
"  total: \"number\",\n"
"},\n"
"\n"
"provider: async () => {\n"
"  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/items\");\n"
"  const data = await res.json();\n"
"  return {\n"
"    entries: [{\n"
"      items: data.results.map((r: any) => ({ name: r.name, count: "
"r.count })),\n"
"      total: data.total,\n"
"    }],\n"
"  };\n"
"},\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"entryFields: {\n"
"  items: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"object\", fields: { name: "
"\"string\", count: \"number\" } } },\n"
"  total: \"number\",\n"
"},\n"
"\n"
"provider: async () => {\n"
"  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/items\");\n"
"  const data = await res.json();\n"
"  return {\n"
"    entries: [{\n"
"      items: data.results.map((r: any) => ({ name: r.name, count: "
"r.count })),\n"
"      total: data.total,\n"
"    }],\n"
"  };\n"
"},\n"
"```"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:179
msgid ""
"If the fetch fails or JSON parsing throws, the widget extension falls back "
"to the placeholder data:"
msgstr ""
"Si la récupération échoue ou si le parsing JSON lève une exception, "
"l'extension de widget se replie sur les données placeholder :"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:181
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"Widget({\n"
"  // ...\n"
"  placeholder: { temperature: 0, condition: \"Loading...\" },\n"
"\n"
"  provider: async () => {\n"
"    const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/weather\");\n"
"    if (!res.ok) {\n"
"      // Return stale/fallback data with a short retry interval\n"
"      return {\n"
"        entries: [{ temperature: 0, condition: \"Unavailable\" }],\n"
"        reloadPolicy: { after: { minutes: 5 } },\n"
"      };\n"
"    }\n"
"    const data = await res.json();\n"
"    return {\n"
"      entries: [{ temperature: data.temp, condition: data.desc }],\n"
"      reloadPolicy: { after: { minutes: 15 } },\n"
"    };\n"
"  },\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"Widget({\n"
"  // ...\n"
"  placeholder: { temperature: 0, condition: \"Loading...\" },\n"
"\n"
"  provider: async () => {\n"
"    const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/weather\");\n"
"    if (!res.ok) {\n"
"      // Return stale/fallback data with a short retry interval\n"
"      return {\n"
"        entries: [{ temperature: 0, condition: \"Unavailable\" }],\n"
"        reloadPolicy: { after: { minutes: 5 } },\n"
"      };\n"
"    }\n"
"    const data = await res.json();\n"
"    return {\n"
"      entries: [{ temperature: data.temp, condition: data.desc }],\n"
"      reloadPolicy: { after: { minutes: 15 } },\n"
"    };\n"
"  },\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:204
msgid ""
"The `placeholder` field provides data shown in the widget gallery and during "
"loading. If the provider throws an unhandled exception, the generated Swift/"
"Kotlin code catches it and renders the placeholder instead."
msgstr ""
"Le champ `placeholder` fournit les données affichées dans la galerie de "
"widgets et pendant le chargement. Si le provider lève une exception non "
"gérée, le code Swift/Kotlin généré la capture et affiche le placeholder à la "
"place."

#: src/widgets/data-fetching.md:206
msgid ""
"Note that with two distinct literal policies (5 and 15 minutes above), the "
"compiled widget uses the smaller one — 5 minutes, which the platform floor "
"then raises to its minimum (15 minutes on iOS) — and the compiler warns "
"about the choice. See [Reload Policies](#reload-policies)."
msgstr ""
"Notez qu'avec deux polices littérales distinctes (5 et 15 minutes ci-"
"dessus), le widget compilé utilise le plus petit  5 minutes, que le plancher "
"de la plate-forme augmente ensuite à son minimum (15 minutes sur iOS)  et le "
"compilateur prévient sur le choix. Voir [Politiques de rechargement](#reload-"
"policies)."

