"The output names the owning package, the call kind, the source span, and the "
"missing token — enough to either (a) extend the allow-list, (b) set `\"*\": "
"[\"<token>\"]` for a wider default, or (c) replace the dep with one that "
"doesn't need the capability."
msgstr ""
"La sortie indique le package propriétaire, le type d'appel, l'emplacement "
"dans le source et le token manquant — suffisant pour soit (a) étendre la "
"liste d'autorisation, (b) définir `\"*\": [\"<token>\"]` pour un défaut plus "
"large, ou (c) remplacer la dépendance par une qui n'a pas besoin de cette "
"capacité."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:82
msgid "Recommended workflow"
msgstr "Workflow recommandé"

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:84
msgid ""
"**Start empty.** Set `\"permissions\": {}` to confirm your build is "
"currently passing without the pass active."
msgstr ""
"**Commencer à vide.** Définir `\"permissions\": {}` pour confirmer que votre "
"build passe actuellement sans le pass actif."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:86
msgid ""
"**Flip the default to deny.** Add `\"*\": []` and rebuild. The diagnostic "
"enumerates every capability your dep tree currently reaches."
msgstr ""
"**Basculer le défaut en refus.** Ajouter `\"*\": []` et reconstruire. Le "
"diagnostic énumère toutes les capacités que votre arbre de dépendances "
"atteint actuellement."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:89
msgid ""
"**Grant minimum tokens per dep.** Use the diagnostic to populate "
"`permissions` with the smallest token set each package needs."
msgstr ""
"**Accorder les tokens minimaux par dépendance.** Utiliser le diagnostic pour "
"renseigner `permissions` avec le plus petit ensemble de tokens dont chaque "
"package a besoin."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:91
msgid ""
"**Lock in CI.** Once the build is green with the explicit permissions, leave "
"it that way — new deps that want new tokens show up as build failures, "
"surfacing in the PR review."
msgstr ""
"**Verrouiller en CI.** Une fois le build au vert avec les permissions "
"explicites, le laisser ainsi — les nouvelles dépendances réclamant de "
"nouveaux tokens apparaissent comme des échecs de build, et sont visibles "
"lors de la revue de PR."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:95
msgid "Relationship to other security flags"
msgstr "Relation avec les autres flags de sécurité"

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:97
msgid ""
"**`--lockdown` (#496)** — gates host code itself against the arbitrary-code-"
"execution surfaces (perry-jsruntime, `perry.nativeLibrary` archives, "
"`child_process.*`). Orthogonal: `perry.permissions` is per-dep, `--lockdown` "
"is whole-binary."
msgstr ""
"**`--lockdown` (#496)** — protège le code hôte lui-même contre les surfaces "
"d'exécution de code arbitraire (perry-jsruntime, archives "
"`perry.nativeLibrary`, `child_process.*`). Orthogonal : `perry.permissions` "
"est par dépendance, `--lockdown` est pour l'ensemble du binaire."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:101
msgid ""
"**`allowedHosts` (#502)** — narrows `net:fetch` from \"any URL\" to \"URLs "
"matching this allow-list.\" A dep with `net:fetch` permission still has to "
"clear the egress allow-list at every call site."
msgstr ""
"**`allowedHosts` (#502)** — restreint `net:fetch` de « toute URL » à « URLs "
"correspondant à cette liste d'autorisation ». Une dépendance avec la "
"permission `net:fetch` doit tout de même passer la liste d'autorisation de "
"sortie à chaque site d'appel."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:104
msgid ""
"**`PERRY_SANDBOX_BUILDRS` (#505)** — sandboxes the _build-time_ `build.rs` "
"scripts. `perry.permissions` controls what the _runtime_ binary can do."
msgstr ""
"**`PERRY_SANDBOX_BUILDRS` (#505)** — isole les scripts `build.rs` au _moment "
"de la compilation_. `perry.permissions` contrôle ce que le binaire peut "
"faire à l'_exécution_."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:110
msgid ""
"[`#501`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/501) — design discussion."
msgstr ""
"[`#501`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/501) — discussion de "
"conception."

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:111
msgid "[`--lockdown`](./lockdown.md)"
msgstr "[`--lockdown`](./lockdown.md)"

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:112
msgid "[Egress Allowlist (`allowedHosts`)](./allowed-hosts.md)"
msgstr "[Liste d'autorisation de sortie (`allowedHosts`)](./allowed-hosts.md)"

#: src/cli/capabilities.md:113
msgid "[`PERRY_SANDBOX_BUILDRS`](./sandbox-buildrs.md)"
msgstr "[`PERRY_SANDBOX_BUILDRS`](./sandbox-buildrs.md)"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:1
msgid "Behavioral SBOM (`perry audit --sbom`)"
msgstr "SBOM comportemental (`perry audit --sbom`)"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:3
msgid ""
"Every Perry compile writes a behavioral SBOM to `audit.json` in the "
"project's cache dir (default `<project>/node_modules/.cache/perry/"
"audit.json`) — a per-module manifest of the stdlib symbols the build "
"actually calls. The manifest is the foundation for the rest of the supply-"
"chain hardening series and gives reviewers a way to see exactly what surface "
"a dependency touches without rebuilding the binary."
msgstr ""
"Chaque compilation Perry écrit un SBOM comportemental à `audit.json` dans le "
"cache du projet (par défaut `<project>/node_modules/.cache/perry/"
"audit.json`)  un manifeste par module des symboles stdlib que la compilation "
"appelle réellement. Le manifeste est la base pour le reste de la série de "
"durcissement de la chaîne d'approvisionnement et donne aux examinateurs un "
"moyen de voir exactement quelle surface une dépendance touche sans "
"reconstruire le binaire."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:11
msgid ""
"**Zero runtime cost.** The walk runs at compile time over the lowered HIR; "
"the file is written observationally and a missing-directory error never "
"fails the build."
msgstr ""
"**Aucun coût à l'exécution.** Le parcours s'effectue au moment de la "
"compilation sur le HIR abaissé ; le fichier est écrit de manière "
"observationnelle et une erreur de répertoire manquant ne fait jamais échouer "
"le build."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:15
msgid "What's recorded"
msgstr "Ce qui est enregistré"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:17
msgid "For each source module:"
msgstr "Pour chaque module source :"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:19
msgid "**`source`** — canonical path the module was lowered from."
msgstr "**`source`** — chemin canonique depuis lequel le module a été abaissé."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:20
msgid ""
"**`package`** — owning npm package name when the source lives under "
"`node_modules/<pkg>/...` (scope-aware: `@scope/pkg`). `null` for host source."
msgstr ""
"**`package`** — nom du package npm propriétaire lorsque le source se trouve "
"sous `node_modules/<pkg>/...` (avec prise en compte des scopes : `@scope/"
"pkg`). `null` pour le source hôte."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:23
msgid ""
"**`stdlib`** — map of `<namespace>` → sorted unique method names. Captures "
"both the general-shape `NativeMethodCall` lowering "
"(`mysql2.createConnection`, `child_process.execSync`, …) and the dedicated "
"specialized variants Perry uses for hot paths (`fs.readFileSync`, "
"`path.join`, `process.env`, `tty.isatty`, `url.fileURLToPath`, …)."
msgstr ""
"**`stdlib`** — map de `<namespace>` → noms de méthodes uniques triés. "
"Capture à la fois l'abaissement générique `NativeMethodCall` "
"(`mysql2.createConnection`, `child_process.execSync`, …) et les variantes "
"spécialisées dédiées que Perry utilise pour les chemins chauds "
"(`fs.readFileSync`, `path.join`, `process.env`, `tty.isatty`, "
"`url.fileURLToPath`, …)."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:32
msgid "A `main.ts` like:"
msgstr "Un `main.ts` comme :"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:34
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import * as fs from \"fs\";\n"
"import * as path from \"path\";\n"
"\n"
"const data = fs.readFileSync(\"/etc/hostname\", \"utf8\");\n"
"const p = path.join(\"/tmp\", \"x\");\n"
"console.log(data, p);\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import * as fs from \"fs\";\n"
"import * as path from \"path\";\n"
"\n"
"const data = fs.readFileSync(\"/etc/hostname\", \"utf8\");\n"
"const p = path.join(\"/tmp\", \"x\");\n"
"console.log(data, p);\n"
"```"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:43
msgid "produces:"
msgstr "produit :"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:48
msgid "\"modules\""
msgstr "\"modules\""

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:50
msgid "\"/repo/main.ts\""
msgstr "\"/repo/main.ts\""

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:52
msgid "\"stdlib\""
msgstr "\"stdlib\" est le nom de l'application"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:53
msgid "\"fs\""
msgstr "\"F\""

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:53
msgid "\"readFileSync\""
msgstr "\"readFileSync\""

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:54
msgid "\"path\""
msgstr "\"chemin\""

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:54
msgid "\"join\""
msgstr "\"joindre\""

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:61
msgid ""
"The JSON output is byte-deterministic across builds (BTreeMap keys + sorted "
"method lists), so `perry audit --sbom > before.txt` + a `package.json` "
"change + a re-build + `perry audit --sbom > after.txt`"
msgstr ""
"La sortie JSON est déterministe au niveau des octets entre les builds (clés "
"BTreeMap + listes de méthodes triées), de sorte que `perry audit --sbom > "
"before.txt` + une modification de `package.json` + une reconstruction + "
"`perry audit --sbom > after.txt`"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:64
msgid ""
"`diff before.txt after.txt` is a meaningful review tool — any new capability "
"a dependency reaches surfaces as added lines."
msgstr ""
"`diff before.txt after.txt` est un outil de revue pertinent — toute nouvelle "
"capacité qu'une dépendance atteint apparaît sous forme de lignes ajoutées."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:67
msgid "CLI"
msgstr "CLI"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:69
msgid "`perry audit --sbom [PATH]`"
msgstr "`perry audit --sbom [PATH]`"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:71
msgid ""
"Reads the manifest from `audit.json` in the resolved cache dir (default "
"`<PATH>/node_modules/.cache/perry/audit.json`; honors `--cache-dir` / "
"`PERRY_CACHE_DIR` / perry.toml `[perry] cacheDir` / package.json "
"`perry.cacheDir`), walking up the directory tree if needed (same shape "
"`perry compile` walks up to find `package.json`)."
msgstr ""
"Lire le manifeste de `audit.json` dans le répertoire de cache résolu (par "
"défaut `<PATH>/node_modules/.cache/perry/audit.json`; honore `--cache-dir` / "
"`PERRY_CACHE_DIR` / perry.toml `[perry] cacheDir` / package.json "
"`perry.cacheDir`), en remontant l'arbre de répertoire si nécessaire (même "
"forme `perry compile` marche vers le haut pour trouver `package.json`)."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:77
msgid "Default `PATH`: current directory."
msgstr "`PATH` par défaut : répertoire courant."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:78
msgid "In `--format json` mode dumps the raw manifest pretty-printed."
msgstr "En mode `--format json`, affiche le manifeste brut mis en forme."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:79
msgid ""
"In text mode groups modules by owning npm package; host source is reported "
"under `<host source>`."
msgstr ""
"En mode texte, regroupe les modules par package npm propriétaire ; le source "
"hôte est signalé sous `<host source>`."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:81
msgid ""
"Returns a clear error if the manifest doesn't exist yet — `perry  compile` "
"or `perry run` writes it on every successful build."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie une erreur claire si le manifeste n'existe pas encore  `perry  "
"compile` ou `perry run` l'écrit sur chaque build réussi."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:84
msgid "What's NOT yet recorded"
msgstr "Ce qui n'est PAS encore enregistré"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:86
msgid "Scope of this first cut (MVP):"
msgstr "Périmètre de cette première version (MVP) :"

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:88
msgid ""
"**Literal `fetch` / `http.get` URLs** — the compiler can enforce these "
"through [`allowedHosts`](allowed-hosts.md), implemented by closed issue "
"[`#502`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/502), but audit manifest v1 "
"does not project them into a `literal_hosts` field."
msgstr ""
"**Les URL `fetch` / `http.get` littérales** le compilateur peut les "
"appliquer par [`allowedHosts`](allowed-hosts.md), implémenté par la version "
"fermée [`#502`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/502), mais le "
"manifeste d'audit v1 ne les projette pas dans un champ `literal_hosts`."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:92
msgid ""
"**Native-library symbol references** (FFI registry) — the registry exists in "
"codegen, but audit manifest v1 does not project it into a `native_symbols` "
"field."
msgstr ""
"**Références de symboles natifs de bibliothèque** (Registre FFI)  le "
"registre existe dans codegen, mais le manifeste d'audit v1 ne le projette "
"pas dans un champ `native_symbols`."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:95
msgid ""
"**`perry audit --sbom --diff`** — the bytes-deterministic JSON shape already "
"enables the diff workflow via plain `diff` / `git diff`; a built-in `--diff` "
"is a follow-up that picks a baseline (`audit.last.json` in the cache dir) "
"and pretty-prints the change set."
msgstr ""
"**`perry audit --sbom --diff`** la forme JSON déterministe en octets permet "
"déjà le flux de travail différentiel via `diff` / `git diff`; un `--diff` "
"intégré est un suivi qui choisit une ligne de base (`audit.last.json` dans "
"le répertoire de cache) et imprime l'ensemble des modifications."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:101
msgid ""
"The manifest shape is versioned (`version: 1`) so consumers can detect when "
"new top-level keys land."
msgstr ""
"La forme du manifeste est versionnée (`version: 1`) afin que les "
"consommateurs puissent détecter l'ajout de nouvelles clés de premier niveau."

#: src/cli/perry-audit-sbom.md:106
msgid ""
"[`#495`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/495) — design discussion."
msgstr ""
"[`#495`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/495) — discussion de "
"conception."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:1
msgid "Host Allowlist for `nativeLibrary` and `compilePackages`"
msgstr "Liste d'autorisation hôte pour `nativeLibrary` et `compilePackages`"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:3
msgid ""
"Perry refuses to honor two privileged dependency features — the two attack "
"surfaces Perry itself introduced over Node — unless the host application has "
"explicitly opted in to each consumer:"
msgstr ""
"Perry refuse d'honorer deux fonctionnalités de dépendances privilégiées — "
"les deux surfaces d'attaque que Perry lui-même a introduites par rapport à "
"Node — sauf si l'application hôte a explicitement accepté chaque "
"consommateur :"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:7
msgid ""
"`perry.nativeLibrary` — a transitive dep linking arbitrary native code into "
"the binary."
msgstr ""
"`perry.nativeLibrary` — une dépendance transitive liant du code natif "
"arbitraire dans le binaire."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:9
msgid ""
"`perry.compilePackages` — compiling untrusted TS source from an npm package "
"into the binary as if it were first-party code."
msgstr ""
"`perry.compilePackages` — compilation du source TypeScript non fiable d'un "
"package npm dans le binaire comme s'il s'agissait de code interne."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:12
msgid "Both checks fire at compile time. **Zero runtime cost.**"
msgstr ""
"Les deux vérifications se déclenchent au moment de la compilation. **Aucun "
"coût à l'exécution.**"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:16
msgid "`nativeLibrary` (transitive dep declares it)"
msgstr "`nativeLibrary` (déclaré par une dépendance transitive)"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:18
msgid ""
"A package shipped with `perry.nativeLibrary` in its own `package.json` is "
"detected during dependency collection. Without an entry in the host's "
"`perry.allow.nativeLibrary`, the build fails:"
msgstr ""
"Un package livré avec `perry.nativeLibrary` dans son propre `package.json` "
"est détecté lors de la collecte des dépendances. Sans entrée dans "
"`perry.allow.nativeLibrary` de l'hôte, le build échoue :"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:22
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"Error: package `@bloomengine/engine` declares `perry.nativeLibrary`\n"
"(links arbitrary native code into the binary) but is not in your host\n"
"`perry.allow.nativeLibrary`. Review the package, then add it to your\n"
"host `package.json`:\n"
"\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"perry\": {\n"
"      \"allow\": { \"nativeLibrary\": [\"@bloomengine/engine\"] }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"Error: package `@bloomengine/engine` declares `perry.nativeLibrary`\n"
"(links arbitrary native code into the binary) but is not in your host\n"
"`perry.allow.nativeLibrary`. Review the package, then add it to your\n"
"host `package.json`:\n"
"\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"perry\": {\n"
"      \"allow\": { \"nativeLibrary\": [\"@bloomengine/engine\"] }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
"```"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:35
msgid "`compilePackages` (host or workspace root declares it)"
msgstr "`compilePackages` (déclaré par l'hôte ou la racine du workspace)"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:37
msgid ""
"Every entry in `perry.compilePackages` must also be matched by an entry in "
"`perry.allow.compilePackages` — a two-key opt-in:"
msgstr ""
"Chaque entrée dans `perry.compilePackages` doit également correspondre à une "
"entrée dans `perry.allow.compilePackages` — un opt-in à deux clés :"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:48
msgid "1. Host `package.json` (persistent, recommended)"
msgstr "1. `package.json` hôte (persistant, recommandé)"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:57
msgid "\"@bloomengine/engine\""
msgstr "\"@bloomengine/engine\""

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:63
msgid "2. Scope wildcard"
msgstr "2. Joker de scope"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:65
msgid "`\"@scope/*\"` matches any package under `@scope/`:"
msgstr "`\"@scope/*\"` correspond à tout package sous `@scope/` :"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:71
msgid "\"@nestjs/*\""
msgstr "\"@nestjs/*\""

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:71
msgid "\"reflect-metadata\""
msgstr "\"méta-données de réflexion\""

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:71
msgid "\"rxjs\""
msgstr "\"rxjs\""

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:77
msgid "3. Universal escape hatch"
msgstr "3. Échappatoire universelle"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:79
msgid ""
"`\"*\"` matches every name. Use sparingly — defeats the purpose of the "
"allowlist."
msgstr ""
"`\"*\"` correspond à tous les noms. À utiliser avec parcimonie — cela annule "
"l'intérêt de la liste d'autorisation."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:86
msgid "4. Environment variable"
msgstr "4. Variable d'environnement"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:88
msgid ""
"`PERRY_ALLOW_PERRY_FEATURES=1` opts every package into both allowlists for "
"the current build — emergency knob for one-off builds where editing "
"`package.json` isn't an option. `=0` enforces refusal even when "
"`package.json` opted in (fail-closed CI gate)."
msgstr ""
"`PERRY_ALLOW_PERRY_FEATURES=1` autorise tous les packages dans les deux "
"listes d'autorisation pour la build en cours — commande d'urgence pour les "
"builds ponctuelles où la modification de `package.json` n'est pas possible. "
"`=0` impose le refus même si `package.json` a opté (verrou CI fail-closed)."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:93
msgid "Default-deny rationale"
msgstr "Raison du refus par défaut"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:95
msgid "Both features escape Perry's structural guarantees:"
msgstr ""
"Les deux fonctionnalités contournent les garanties structurelles de Perry :"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:97
msgid ""
"`nativeLibrary` lets a transitive dep ship arbitrary machine code that runs "
"at the same trust level as the host application."
msgstr ""
"`nativeLibrary` permet à une dépendance transitive de livrer du code machine "
"arbitraire s'exécutant au même niveau de confiance que l'application hôte."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:99
msgid ""
"`compilePackages` runs the dep's TypeScript through Perry's full native "
"pipeline (HIR / codegen / linker) instead of routing it through QuickJS, "
"eliminating the runtime sandbox."
msgstr ""
"`compilePackages` fait passer le TypeScript de la dépendance par le pipeline "
"natif complet de Perry (HIR / codegen / linker) au lieu de le router via "
"QuickJS, supprimant ainsi le sandbox d'exécution."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:103
msgid ""
"Both are useful features, but they're _privileged_ operations. The allowlist "
"makes that privilege explicit and auditable: a reviewer diffing a PR can see "
"exactly which deps have been granted native access, and `git blame` records "
"who approved each one."
msgstr ""
"Ces deux fonctionnalités sont utiles, mais il s'agit d'opérations "
"_privilégiées_. La liste d'autorisation rend ce privilège explicite et "
"auditable : un relecteur qui examine une PR peut voir exactement quelles "
"dépendances ont reçu un accès natif, et `git blame` enregistre qui a "
"approuvé chacune d'elles."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:108
msgid "Node native addons are not `compilePackages`"
msgstr "Node native addons are not `compilePackages`"

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:110
msgid ""
"`compilePackages` does not support npm packages whose JavaScript entry point "
"loads a Node native addon. Markers include `.node` files, `binding.gyp`, "
"`prebuilds/`, and `\"gypfile\"` in `package.json`."
msgstr ""
"`compilePackages` ne prend pas en charge les paquets npm dont le point "
"d'entrée JavaScript charge un addon natif de Node. Les marqueurs incluent "
"les fichiers `.node`, `binding.gyp`, `prebuilds/` et `\"gypfile\"` dans "
"`package.json`."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:114
msgid ""
"Those packages are not just JavaScript with a dynamic `require()`. Their "
"native binary expects Node's addon ABI: Node-API/N-API, NAN, V8, libuv, or "
"Node internals. Perry does not host that ABI through `compilePackages`, so "
"the compiler rejects these packages early when they are opted into "
"`perry.compilePackages`."
msgstr ""
"Ces paquets ne sont pas seulement JavaScript avec un `require()` dynamique. "
"Leur binaire natif s'attend à l'addon ABI de Node: Node-API/N-API, NAN, V8, "
"libuv, ou les internes de Node. Perry n'héberge pas cet ABI via "
"`compilePackages`, de sorte que le compilateur rejette ces paquets tôt quand "
"ils sont optés dans `perry.compilePackages`."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:120
msgid ""
"Use `perry.nativeLibrary` for supported native code instead. A Perry-native "
"replacement should be a thin binding around the native boundary, with "
"unsupported targets declared explicitly in the native-library manifest."
msgstr ""
"Utilisez `perry.nativeLibrary` pour le code natif pris en charge. Un "
"remplacement Perry-native devrait être un lien mince autour de la frontière "
"native, avec des cibles non soutenues déclarées explicitement dans le "
"manifeste native-library."

#: src/cli/allow-perry-features.md:127
msgid ""
"[`#497`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/497) — design discussion."
msgstr ""
"[`#497`](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/497) — discussion de "
"conception."

#: src/cli/perry-toml.md:3
msgid ""
"`perry.toml` is the project-level configuration file for Perry. It controls "
"project metadata, build settings, platform-specific options, code signing, "
"distribution, auditing, and verification."
msgstr ""
"`perry.toml` est le fichier de configuration au niveau du projet pour Perry. "
"Il contrôle les métadonnées du projet, les paramètres de build, les options "
"spécifiques à chaque plateforme, la signature de code, la distribution, "
"l'audit et la vérification."

#: src/cli/perry-toml.md:5
msgid ""
"Created automatically by `perry init`, it lives at the root of your project "
"alongside `package.json`."
msgstr ""
"Créé automatiquement par `perry init`, il se trouve à la racine de votre "
"projet, aux côtés de `package.json`."

#: src/cli/perry-toml.md:7
msgid "Minimal Example"
msgstr "Exemple minimal"

#: src/cli/perry-toml.md:9
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[project]\n"
"name = \"my-app\"\n"
"entry = \"src/main.ts\"\n"
"\n"
"[build]\n"
"out_dir = \"dist\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```toml\n"
"[project]\n"
"name = \"my-app\"\n"
"entry = \"src/main.ts\"\n"
"\n"
"[build]\n"
"out_dir = \"dist\"\n"
"```"

#: src/cli/perry-toml.md:18
msgid "Full Example"
msgstr "Exemple complet"

#: src/cli/perry-toml.md:20
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[project]\n"
"name = \"my-app\"\n"
"version = \"1.2.0\"\n"
"build_number = 42\n"
"bundle_id = \"com.example.myapp\"\n"
"description = \"A cross-platform Perry application\"\n"
"entry = \"src/main.ts\"\n"
"\n"
"[project.icons]\n"
"source = \"assets/icon.png\"\n"
"\n"
"[build]\n"
"out_dir = \"dist\"\n"
"\n"
"[macos]\n"
"bundle_id = \"com.example.myapp.macos\"\n"
"category = \"public.app-category.developer-tools\"\n"
"minimum_os = \"13.0\"\n"
"entitlements = [\"com.apple.security.network.client\"]\n"
"distribute = \"both\"\n"
"signing_identity = \"Developer ID Application: My Company (TEAMID)\"\n"
"certificate = \"certs/mac-appstore.p12\"\n"
"notarize_certificate = \"certs/mac-devid.p12\"\n"
"notarize_signing_identity = \"Developer ID Application: My Company (TEAMID)"
"\"\n"
"installer_certificate = \"certs/mac-installer.p12\"\n"
"team_id = \"ABCDE12345\"\n"
"key_id = \"KEYID123\"\n"
"issuer_id = \"issuer-uuid-here\"\n"
"p8_key_path = \"certs/AuthKey.p8\"\n"
"encryption_exempt = true\n"
"\n"
"[ios]\n"
"bundle_id = \"com.example.myapp.ios\"\n"
"deployment_target = \"16.0\"\n"
"device_family = [\"iphone\", \"ipad\"]\n"
"orientations = [\"portrait\", \"landscape-left\", \"landscape-right\"]\n"
"capabilities = [\"push-notification\"]\n"
"distribute = \"appstore\"\n"
"entry = \"src/main-ios.ts\"\n"
"provisioning_profile = \"certs/MyApp.mobileprovision\"\n"
"certificate = \"certs/ios-distribution.p12\"\n"
"signing_identity = \"iPhone Distribution: My Company (TEAMID)\"\n"
"team_id = \"ABCDE12345\"\n"
"key_id = \"KEYID123\"\n"
"issuer_id = \"issuer-uuid-here\"\n"
"p8_key_path = \"certs/AuthKey.p8\"\n"
"encryption_exempt = true\n"
"\n"
"[android]\n"
"package_name = \"com.example.myapp\"\n"
"min_sdk = \"26\"\n"
"target_sdk = \"34\"\n"
"permissions = [\"INTERNET\", \"CAMERA\"]\n"
"distribute = \"playstore\"\n"
"keystore = \"certs/release.keystore\"\n"
"key_alias = \"my-key\"\n"
"google_play_key = \"certs/play-service-account.json\"\n"
"entry = \"src/main-android.ts\"\n"
"\n"
"[linux]\n"
"format = \"appimage\"\n"
"category = \"Development\"\n"
"description = \"A cross-platform Perry application\"\n"
"\n"
"[i18n]\n"
"locales = [\"en\", \"de\", \"fr\"]\n"
"default_locale = \"en\"\n"
"\n"
"[i18n.currencies]\n"
"en = \"USD\"\n"
"de = \"EUR\"\n"
"fr = \"EUR\"\n"
"\n"
"[publish]\n"
"server = \"https://hub.perryts.com\"\n"
"exclude = [\"screenshots\", \"docs\"]\n"
"# Deliberately send this input; see the archive safety policy below.\n"
"include = [\".env.publish\"]\n"
"\n"
"[audit]\n"
"fail_on = \"B\"\n"
"severity = \"high\"\n"
"ignore = [\"RULE-001\", \"RULE-002\"]\n"
"\n"
"[verify]\n"
"url = \"https://verify.perryts.com\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
